/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-07T12:04:55-08:00","id":1013891,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1013866-hurt-locker?p=1013888#post1013888\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> They were featured in <a href=\"https://&amp;quot;&#91;url\" target=\"_blank\">http://theonyxpath.com/hurt-locker-open-dev-dump-2/&amp;quot;]open</a> development[/URL].</div> </div> </div> </div>Oh my goodness. Straight into my 1960s conspiracy setting they go.<br /> <br /> I'm a little surprised the Lost Boys didn't get rolled into Deviant, honestly. This books looks a thousand times more fun than I gave it credit for.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-07T12:40:13-08:00","id":1013910,"title":"","content":"Damn... Can't lie, I'm pretty disappointed the Armed to the Teeth Condition I wrote and David said he wanted to put in the book didn't make it in. I assume it must not have been able to fit the wordcount or something.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":269,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","user":"Charlaquin","date":"12-07-2016, 06:46 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-07T12:44:58-08:00","id":1013916,"title":"","content":"I've been waiting to pick Hurt Locker up for a while but I want to see the preview first and the preview is just not loading. I'm really not that interested in new mini-splats or merits, so I'm wondering how much of the book is dedicated to its premise of exploring violence and the effects thereof on the lives of people.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2855-axelgear","name":"Axelgear","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2855_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1450"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-07T12:47:02-08:00","id":1013918,"title":"","content":"I very rarely run across a book that directly addresses ableism like that, especially within storytelling itself. Its an inclusion I didn't know that I wanted, but I am happy its there.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>How can I know if what I claim I know to be true is rejecting the idea that there is something I might not know? How can I know if what I claim I don't know to be true is rejecting the idea that there is something I do know?<br /> -Zhuangzi","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1715-ostarion","name":"Ostarion","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1715_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"305"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-07T13:02:31-08:00","id":1013928,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1013866-hurt-locker?p=1013910#post1013910\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Damn... Can't lie, I'm pretty disappointed the Armed to the Teeth Merit I wrote and David said he wanted to put in the book didn't make it in. I assume it must not have been able to fit the wordcount or something.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Is it possible for you to share it here on the forum? I'm curious despite having two new books to go through.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-07T13:14:19-08:00","id":1013940,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tessie</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1013866-hurt-locker?p=1013928#post1013928\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Is it possible for you to share it here on the forum? I'm curious despite having two new books to go through.</div> </div> </div> </div>For sure, this was where I originally posted it. It's meant to work with the Capacity rules from the weapons appendix, to make tracking &quot;extra reloads&quot; cleaner.<br /> <br /> <u>New Condition - Armed to the Teeth</u><br /> Your character is carrying extra ammunition for her weapon. Pick a specific ranged or thrown weapon when you acquire this Condition. By spending an Instant action and shedding this Condition, you can restore a weapon of that type that has run out of ammunition to full capacity. Shedding the Condition in this way does not grant a Beat. A character can have multiple instances of this Condition, each associated with a different weapon.<br /> <b>Possible Sources:</b> A character can acquire this Condition with a purchase at Availability one less than the Availability of the weapon it is associated with (minimum 1). At Storyteller discretion, a character may be able to get it by other means, such as robbing a sporting goods store or scavenging ammo off of someone equipped with the same type of weapon,<br /> <b>Resolution:</b> Have your ammunition confiscated or stolen.<br /> <b>Beat:</b> n/a<br /> <br /> Loaded for Bear would allow you to reload a weapon without expending Armed to the Teeth a number of times per scene equal to your dots in the Merit.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-07T13:25:29-08:00","id":1013944,"title":"","content":"EDIT: I'm an idiot. I was thinking of Loaded for Bear on page 143.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>My ideas are bad and I should feel bad.","edited":{"userid":12157,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12157-kvark","user":"Kvark","date":". 12-07-2016, 04:28 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12157-kvark","name":"Kvark","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"186"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-07T13:29:40-08:00","id":1013947,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kvark</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1013866-hurt-locker?p=1013944#post1013944\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">There's a merit that does that, it's just named something different. Give me a sec and I'll find it...</div> </div> </div> </div>It's called Loaded for Bear. The point of the Condition isn't to give you extra reloads (which is what Loaded for Bear does), it's to replace the rules for reloads, which currently require you to track reloads as an abstract thing that disappears after a scene. Turning reloads into a Condition just makes them easier to track, functionally it's practically the same as the current rule.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-07T13:36:58-08:00","id":1013955,"title":"","content":"I'm so happy it's finally out and I hope everyone enjoys it as much as we did making it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Will Rotenberry</b><br /> Onyx Path Freelancer<br /> <b>Armory: Hurt Locker</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5031-bloodywillpower","name":"BloodyWillpower","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5031_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-07T13:42:52-08:00","id":1013957,"title":"","content":"At a cursory glance it's fun, and certainly a lot of cool new content. It doesn't seem like there is much in the books that deals with firearms though. Was wondering if there were a conscious choice to omit that from this book (due to wordcount restrictions I'm guessing?).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>My ideas are bad and I should feel bad.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12157-kvark","name":"Kvark","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"186"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-07T14:26:51-08:00","id":1013979,"title":"","content":"I've barely delved into the book and already I'm loving the merits it grants players, particularly for Changeling - Riddle-Kith's Fairest seeming affinity is sometimes difficult to use, as it allows you to grant temporarily merit dots to those affected so they can emulate a particular kith. Problem is that many kiths don't have merits that really represent them...at least until Hurt Locker. Air of Menace works great as an alternative for Ifrit's Psychokinesis (if not both together), Cohesive Unit works well for Playmate, Body As Weapon can work for Bloodbrute (at least in part), and so forth.<br /> <br /> That said, I wonder if certain merits that use Integrity can work with other supernatural traits, such as, well, Clarity. The book mentions an alternative to Integrity with Empath's knowing how a supernatural character without Integrity is feeling, such as a Vampire's Humanity, but what about merits like Support Network? Could a Changeling postphone their Clarity break long enough to call their motley for some assurance?<br /> <br /> Also, the rules for stacking fighting merits: love them.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5803-taidragon","name":"Taidragon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5803_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1038"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-07T14:58:23-08:00","id":1013988,"title":"","content":"The flexibility offered by style tags is an immensely welcome addition, and I'm impressed with how much the mechanics on many of these merits have been cleaned up since the initial drafts. There were a lot of cool ideas that weren't mechanically functional, and that's been comprehensively addressed. I'm a bit bummed that some of my favorite content didn't make the cut, but that's why I saved the drafts.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5328-helmsderp","name":"HelmsDerp","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"652"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-07T15:26:25-08:00","id":1014004,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1013866-hurt-locker?p=1013910#post1013910\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Damn... Can't lie, I'm pretty disappointed the Armed to the Teeth Merit I wrote and David said he wanted to put in the book didn't make it in. I assume it must not have been able to fit the wordcount or something.</div> </div> </div> </div>Do me a favor, and hit me up with an email. MachineIV at gmail. I'm gonna try to see if I can slide it in during errata. The last steps were a little clunky.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>David A Hill Jr </b><br /> Freelance Writer<br /> Independent Game Designer","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/70-machineiv","name":"MachineIV","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar70_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1791"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-07T15:36:44-08:00","id":1014016,"title":"","content":"The sheer glee of some of these settings. &quot;Soon it'll be zero!&quot;<br /> <br /> It's <i>great</i>.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-07T15:45:32-08:00","id":1014024,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MachineIV</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1013866-hurt-locker?p=1014004#post1014004\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Do me a favor, and hit me up with an email. MachineIV at gmail. I'm gonna try to see if I can slide it in during errata. The last steps were a little clunky.</div> </div> </div> </div>Sent. Thank you very much!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-07T15:56:59-08:00","id":1014031,"title":"","content":"Supernatural Resistance, the Merit for all Hunters that can take it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8762-waywardpaladin","name":"WaywardPaladin","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"84"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-07T18:18:05-08:00","id":1014076,"title":"","content":"I'm still really not loving the &quot;+1 Durability (katana) or +1 Initiative (long sword)&quot; feature of the Sword on the new weapons table...","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-07T18:27:54-08:00","id":1014080,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1013866-hurt-locker?p=1014076#post1014076\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm still really not loving the &amp;quot;+1 Durability (katana) or +1 Initiative (long sword)&amp;quot; feature of the Sword on the new weapons table...</div> </div> </div> </div>I might still errata that out.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>David A Hill Jr </b><br /> Freelance Writer<br /> Independent Game Designer","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/70-machineiv","name":"MachineIV","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar70_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1791"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-07T18:53:47-08:00","id":1014089,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MachineIV</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1013866-hurt-locker?p=1014080#post1014080\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I might still errata that out.</div> </div> </div> </div>Please do. It feels kinda ridiculous.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Revlid wrote:<br /> Yes, hollowing out your humanity to become an utterly utilitarian asura is the exact suggestion I would expect from you, Aiden.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/168-aiden","name":"Aiden","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar168_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1431"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-07T19:16:19-08:00","id":1014097,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aiden</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1013866-hurt-locker?p=1014089#post1014089\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Please do. It feels kinda ridiculous.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I have mixed feelings. Good swords are like candy, with a brittle edge and a softer, chewy (okay, not chewy, but candy!) interior. I mean I can see a katana being tougher by virtue of its shape, but this is more a function of shape and not the magical qualities of a katana. But a longsword is . . . uh, longer, and longer weapons really do help determine who gets the first shot in. So maybe this is more a function of weapon length regardless of the sword's uh, nationality. So an arming sword (what people call a &quot;longsword&quot; in RPGs but isn't) or katana or cutlass get the Durability bonus, while a two handed actual-longsword gets the Initiative bonus.<br /> <br /> EDIT: Yeah, I know a katana is used with two hands but at least by the time of Edo-period standardization it's shorter than a longsword. So it's not the handedness, just blade length. Funny thing is right now I'm researching English longsword and Silver recommends the same blade length for a one or two handed weapon, which makes a later English longsword kinda katana-like in its dimensions.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Writer, Game Designer, Pro since 99.<br /> <br /> Thoughts at <a href=\"http://mobunited.com\" target=\"_blank\">mobunited.com</a></b>","edited":{"userid":164,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/164-malcolm","user":"Malcolm","date":". 12-07-2016, 10:20 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/164-malcolm","name":"Malcolm","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar164_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"306"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-07T19:21:18-08:00","id":1014099,"title":"","content":"I came out of Hurt Locker feeling like it was good on the whole, with some weirdness.<br /> <br /> Berserker Style is still a hot mess, though.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2855-axelgear","name":"Axelgear","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2855_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1450"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-07T19:23:34-08:00","id":1014102,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Malcolm</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1013866-hurt-locker?p=1014097#post1014097\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I have mixed feelings. Good swords are like candy, with a brittle edge and a softer, chewy (okay, not chewy, but candy!) interior. I mean I can see a katana being tougher by virtue of its shape, but this is more a function of shape and not the magical qualities of a katana. But a longsword is . . . uh, longer, and longer weapons really do help determine who gets the first shot in. So maybe this is more a function of weapon length regardless of the sword's uh, nationality. So an arming sword (what people call a &quot;longsword&quot; in RPGs but isn't) or katana or cutlass get the Durability bonus, while a two handed actual-longsword gets the Initiative bonus.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, the sword in question has a Strength requirement of 2 and does not have the two-handed quality. So, seems like we're not talking about something that resembles the actual-longsword variety of longsword. Or a Katana, for that matter.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-07T19:37:22-08:00","id":1014104,"title":"","content":"Can I say, I love the Tek-Tek and her barter-a-life train station?<br /> <br /> I'm already planning out a Tokyo Chronicle revolving around her and the kishamono. I also actually like how they cleared up whether or not she's a ghost or not-she explicitly <i>is </i>an actual onryo, but one with her own unique quirks (her kindness and desire to prevent suicides) and a nice purview of what geister are going to be like when 2E comes out (also, answering the question that nobody thought to ask: What Happens When A Different Supernatural Being Hijacks the God-Machine? ...okay, maybe not the G-M explicitly, but she has the mechanical thematics and <i>did </i>explicitly play with the &quot;secret machinery of the world.&quot; She's probably friends with at least one Ring, both because she makes the trains safe so long as they follow her life-editing protocol alone and because they want the Covers that kishamono are too impulsive to not part with). Also a good example of how cults in the CofD form-some supernatural being needs moral help to clean up her mess, she finds someone who sees her favor as miraculous in origin and may not be wrong.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.us/a/img824/1346/mosz.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/180-leliel","name":"Leliel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar180_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-07T20:36:44-08:00","id":1014127,"title":"","content":"So, a couple of things that don't feel like strictly errata but I still want to mention before the final version goes to print:<br /> <br /> Psychokinetic Combat 3, Trapped Potential, doesn't specify a size limit on the objects you can detonate. The text pretty clearly implies that it's meant for size 0-3, given that the examples are a lighter or a welding torch, the damage is limited to three bashing, and the resulting Force is Size 3, but I could see someone trying to use it on a truck, which seems beyond the scope of intent but within the rule as currently written. (Or more humorously: &quot;I blow up... THE EARTH&quot;)<br /> <br /> Sojourner is a neat upgrade to apportation, but while I assume it's intended to remove the drawback it doesn't say so. Thus, teleporting a person one mile would deal 1760 bashing, making it an extremely potent killing power but useless for its (presumably) intended function.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5328-helmsderp","name":"HelmsDerp","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"652"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-07T20:39:38-08:00","id":1014128,"title":"","content":"Those are probably errata enough you should put them in the errata thread.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-07T20:40:45-08:00","id":1014129,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>HelmsDerp</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1013866-hurt-locker?p=1014127#post1014127\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So, a couple of things that don't feel like strictly errata but I still want to mention before the final version goes to print:<br /> <br /> Psychokinetic Combat 3, Trapped Potential, doesn't specify a size limit on the objects you can detonate. The text pretty clearly implies that it's meant for size 0-3, given that the examples are a lighter or a welding torch, the damage is limited to three bashing, and the resulting Force is Size 3, but I could see someone trying to use it on a truck, which seems beyond the scope of intent but within the rule as currently written. (Or more humorously: &quot;I blow up... THE EARTH&quot;)<br /> <br /> Sojourner is a neat upgrade to apportation, but while I assume it's intended to remove the drawback it doesn't say so. Thus, teleporting a person one mile would deal 1760 bashing, making it an extremely potent killing power but useless for its (presumably) intended function.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, go ahead and drop those in the errata thread, and I'll look at cleaning them up a little if I can.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>David A Hill Jr </b><br /> Freelance Writer<br /> Independent Game Designer","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/70-machineiv","name":"MachineIV","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar70_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1791"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-07T23:25:06-08:00","id":1014183,"title":"","content":"The Agony Tilt description lack too, i am too curious...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"","name":"Guest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/default_avatar_large.png","title":"","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-07T23:32:57-08:00","id":1014188,"title":"","content":"If I have Psychokinetic combat 5 and someone punches me while I have corona active and I do the point of lethal damage to them do I gain a wp point?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1383-yrtalien","name":"yrtalien","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"97"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-08T01:14:56-08:00","id":1014207,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>yrtalien</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1013866-hurt-locker?p=1014188#post1014188\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If I have Psychokinetic combat 5 and someone punches me while I have corona active and I do the point of lethal damage to them do I gain a wp point?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I would personally say no in my game due to the obvious abuse it would entail.<br /> <br /> On another note, I do like some of these sidebars for example the one about eschewing labels, very useful advice for the storyteller.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>How can I know if what I claim I know to be true is rejecting the idea that there is something I might not know? How can I know if what I claim I don't know to be true is rejecting the idea that there is something I do know?<br /> -Zhuangzi","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1715-ostarion","name":"Ostarion","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1715_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"305"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-08T02:20:43-08:00","id":1014217,"title":"","content":"Disappointed that the poorly worded language in the Apportation Merit never got cleaned up, despite being pointed out by multiple people.<br /> 'a number of yards per success' is a useless statement, unless we know what that number is.<br /> <br /> Edit: I'm assuming it's one yard, but that seems incredibly low, meaning someone with Resolve 5 (human max) and Occult 5 (again, peak of human ability) would be moving objects...3 yards, on average.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3570-lnodiv","name":"lnodiv","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3570_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1607"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-08T02:44:34-08:00","id":1014223,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>lnodiv</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1013866-hurt-locker?p=1014217#post1014217\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Disappointed that the poorly worded language in the Apportation Merit never got cleaned up, despite being pointed out by multiple people.<br /> 'a number of yards per success' is a useless statement, unless we know what that number is.<br /> <br /> Edit: I'm assuming it's one yard, but that seems incredibly low, meaning someone with Resolve 5 (human max) and Occult 5 (again, peak of human ability) would be moving objects...3 yards, on average.</div> </div> </div> </div>I wasn't able to get to everything. I had limited time to work with. There's still an errata pass to be done.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>David A Hill Jr </b><br /> Freelance Writer<br /> Independent Game Designer","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/70-machineiv","name":"MachineIV","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar70_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1791"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-08T02:47:41-08:00","id":1014224,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MachineIV</s