":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/70-machineiv","name":"MachineIV","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar70_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1791"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-08T07:44:26-08:00","id":1014310,"title":"","content":"In Psychic Onslaught you create a Damage 3, Force 3 explosion with a primary blast area of the psychic\u2019s Resolve. All in all its a pretty tiny blast radius and enemies are only going to take lethal or basing unless the character is hugging them. Since you have to roll the Force rating it turns into ~4L(minus magical armor and all) for people around you, ~4B for yourself, and auto triggering the power even if it maims or kills her. This seems pretty underwhelming for a 5 dot power to be honest... I don't know, maybe I'm missing something?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10769-llegume","name":"LLegume","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"94"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-08T08:19:46-08:00","id":1014321,"title":"","content":"So a couple questions since I see folks are answering. First though I am absolutely loving Hurt Locker, especially the violent skills section. Very very cool stuff. On to my questions though. My group and I were using some of the play test materials that were posted a while ago. One of my players took the Fair Fighter merit and I noticed that that and a few other merits were cut from the final version. I was curious if they were cut for space, balance or tone reasons.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2989-violetdea","name":"violetdea","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-08T13:46:49-08:00","id":1014443,"title":"","content":"I just bought this. If you haven't bought it you should buy it. it should be eventually folded into CoD v3. Even if you don't play CoD it has cool ideas for any modern horror game.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5685-archivist","name":"Archivist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5685_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"363"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-08T14:03:05-08:00","id":1014447,"title":"","content":"As a note, the various Genre Directories for Chronicles of Darkness have been updated with the relevant material from Hurt Locker. As always, they're here: <a href=\"http://www.jessilaurn.com/genredirectories\" target=\"_blank\">http://www.jessilaurn.com/genredirectories</a>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1731-jessilaurn","name":"Jessilaurn","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1731_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"44"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-08T19:36:43-08:00","id":1014578,"title":"","content":"First, Wow, The Armory line books have always been good, and this is just another great addition. The Tag system is awesome, and I really like the &quot;merit templates&quot;. Also, THANK YOU THANK YOU THANK YOU for putting the quick chart reference in the back. What a timesaver those things are! I do have a couple items that look like they need some adjustment.<br /> <br /> The New Merits for Trigger Discipline and Loaded for Bear really should be up in the merits section. My players are never going to be looking for them down on page 143, especially with the quick reference pages for weapons in an appendix. Tilts should also kind of be down with the new Conditions, to try to keep things neat.<br /> <br /> One last thing I wanted to bring up is with The Lost Boys and Serum. It looks like this needs to be looked at and fleshed out just a little more. I love the concept (especially overclocking), but the mechanics are a little bit sparse.<br /> <br /> We know that Serum, (tox 5) is going to do you some damage (great idea, btw). Fixer Serum (the 'knockoff') is Tox 7 because it's &quot;less pure&quot;. Is that the only difference between the two? Are there no other side effects? Does it last just as long as regular Serum?<br /> <br /> I would like to see some sort of general rule for people who try to 'ride the wave' with Deprivation. I'm imagining a storyline where some of the implants make their way into students who need a boost in their grades/athletic performance and find out that Deprivation is the 'sweet spot', so operate on half-doses to get the ability to Overclock on-demand 24/7. The students are going to run into the characters of course (they are professors in this chronicle) and basically burn themselves out by staying Deprived for extended periods of time. This lends itself better to some of the merits here than others. Staying Deprived for a long time makes sense when you want to use Augmented Resilience or Augmented Speed because the stat increases are generally going to come out in their favour even with the Deprived Condition knocking down Resistance stats. Even the addition of a cumulative penalty for every period beyond the first that the character stays Deprived might make it work. to balance it out, some of the Deprived costs could be changed from 1L to 2B or something equivalent. <br /> <br /> <br /> Also, why does the Protocol Fixer chart not line up at least roughly with the needs of the user (As presented in the Protocol merit and using Deprived/Withdrawl rules)? Does Delta just rework your system, then leave you with one dose per month, so you can die in less than a day due to augmentation rejection? For example, here are the dots and dosages between Deprived re-ups, Withdrawl re-ups and the amount supplied by the Fixer merit. By the time you reach 3 Protocol dots, you're lagging pretty significantly behind, even if you wait for full withdrawl to set in.Trying to aim for higher Protocol levels is insanity unless your character is lucky enough to be able to churn the stuff out at home on a constant basis.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"b-bbcode__table--wrapper text_table_\"><table class=\"b-bbcode__table text_table\" style=\"border-spacing: 0px; width: 288px\"><tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"><td width=\"64\" class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 0px; padding: 0px\"></td> <td width=\"64\" class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 0px; padding: 0px\">Protocol</td> <td width=\"64\" class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 0px; padding: 0px\"></td> <td width=\"64\" class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 0px; padding: 0px\">Protocol</td> <td width=\"64\" class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 0px; padding: 0px\"></td> <td width=\"64\" class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 0px; padding: 0px\">Protocol Fixer</td> </tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"><td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 0px; padding: 0px\">DOTS</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 0px; padding: 0px\">Dosages needed per month(Re-up at Deprived)</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 0px; padding: 0px\">DOTS</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 0px; padding: 0px\">Dosages needed per month(Re-up at Withdrawl)</td> 