ext_table_xl65\" align=\"right\" style=\"border-width: 0px; padding: 0px\">13.00</td> </tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"><td class=\"text_table_xl65\" align=\"right\" style=\"border-width: 0px; padding: 0px\">4.00</td> <td class=\"text_table_xl65\" align=\"right\" style=\"border-width: 0px; padding: 0px\">60.00</td> <td class=\"text_table_xl65\" align=\"right\" style=\"border-width: 0px; padding: 0px\">4.00</td> <td class=\"text_table_xl65\" align=\"right\" style=\"border-width: 0px; padding: 0px\">30.00</td> <td class=\"text_table_xl65\" align=\"right\" style=\"border-width: 0px; padding: 0px\">3.00</td> <td class=\"text_table_xl65\" align=\"right\" style=\"border-width: 0px; padding: 0px\">25.00</td> </tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"><td class=\"text_table_xl65\" align=\"right\" style=\"border-width: 0px; padding: 0px\">5.00</td> <td class=\"text_table_xl65\" align=\"right\" style=\"border-width: 0px; padding: 0px\">120.00</td> <td class=\"text_table_xl65\" align=\"right\" style=\"border-width: 0px; padding: 0px\">5.00</td> <td class=\"text_table_xl65\" align=\"right\" style=\"border-width: 0px; padding: 0px\">60.00</td> <td class=\"text_table_xl65\" align=\"right\" style=\"border-width: 0px; padding: 0px\">4.00</td> <td class=\"text_table_xl65\" align=\"right\" style=\"border-width: 0px; padding: 0px\">41.00</td> </tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"><td class=\"text_table_xl65\" style=\"border-width: 0px; padding: 0px\"></td> <td class=\"text_table_xl65\" style=\"border-width: 0px; padding: 0px\"></td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 0px; padding: 0px\"></td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 0px; padding: 0px\"></td> <td class=\"text_table_xl65\" align=\"right\" style=\"border-width: 0px; padding: 0px\">5.00</td> <td class=\"text_table_xl65\" align=\"right\" style=\"border-width: 0px; padding: 0px\">57.00</td> </tr> </table></div> (NOTE that in the Protocol Fixer column, as with the chart in the book, the merit starts at 0 with one dose supplied by Delta protocol. That will be in addition to your Fixer contact, hence all of the numbers being 'off' by one.)<br /> <br /> Using the figures above (converted to monthly on a basis of ~4 weeks, 30 days per month) at Protocol 3, with protocol Fixer 3, you would take about 4L from withdrawl before your next 'delivery'. One dot up seems like way too much, but even dots is not enough and gets to death levels at level 5. Ironically, with the way the delivery scale jumps, level 4 is ok, being in Deprivation about ~25-30% of the time overall.<br /> <br /> Again, overall I'm loving the concepts in this book. It's been worth the wait.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5761-shadowjakkal","name":"ShadowJakkal","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-08T22:35:30-08:00","id":1014622,"title":"","content":"I love the violent skills section, I think I found my second favourite line in any gamebook &quot;Drive: Bringing a Car to a Fistfight&quot; (second only to Trenchcoat McNinjasword from Danse Macabre).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6365-fumus","name":"Fumus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6365_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"310"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-09T04:29:42-08:00","id":1014700,"title":"","content":"I loved the opening fiction. Beautifully done.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-09T07:41:35-08:00","id":1014764,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ShadowJakkal</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1013866-hurt-locker?p=1014578#post1014578\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Also, why does the Protocol Fixer chart not line up at least roughly with the needs of the user</div> </div> </div> </div>Does the Delta Protocol sound like a particularly legit operation to you?<br /> <br /> Also, you need to ration the stuff. It takes 2 days to heal a point of lethal damage, so with carefully timed withdrawals you can keep the attrition to a minimum.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3166,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","user":"Elfive","date":". 12-09-2016, 10:45 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-09T08:01:42-08:00","id":1014771,"title":"","content":"Im really happy we got some rules for tilts affecting vampires. Didnt see stunned mentioned though, are they as susceptible to it as everyone else?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?affiliate_id=259490\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/themes/stvault/images/affiliatebanner4.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><br /> <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Christopher%20Falco&amp;affiliate_id=259490\" target=\"_blank\">Storytellers' Vault supplements (WoD, CoD)</a><br /> <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/FalconianP\" target=\"_blank\">My Patreon! (CofD bonuses include: Fae Sorcery/Technomancy for Vampires, Quick Conversion for Inferno, and more!)</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1130-falco1029","name":"falco1029","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1130_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1045"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-09T09:56:20-08:00","id":1014812,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>atamajakki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1013866-hurt-locker?p=1013891#post1013891\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I'm a little surprised the Lost Boys didn't get rolled into Deviant, honestly.</div> </div> </div> </div>I can see that, but...<br /> <br /> With all the technological aspects of their merits, I also got a God-machine vibe from them.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6356-vernuf","name":"vernuf","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-09T10:24:47-08:00","id":1014823,"title":"","content":"Quick question: The second maneuver of the Bowmanship style, Bullseye, states, &quot;When attacking a speci- fied target you may lower your bow\u2019s damage rating to any amount (0 or greater) to add +1 and the 8-again quality to the attack roll.&quot; Is there any reason you would want to reduce the damage rating by more than one? Or is it supposed to add +1 to hit for each point of damage rating you remove?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-09T10:39:05-08:00","id":1014832,"title":"","content":"My guess is that's either what they meant, or what they initially intended before changing their mind and nerfing the ability without properly editing it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-09T11:09:09-08:00","id":1014846,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Elfive</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1013866-hurt-locker?p=1014832#post1014832\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">My guess is that's either what they meant, or what they initially intended before changing their mind and nerfing the ability without properly editing it.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's what I figured. I'll drop it in the errata thread.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-09T13:49:26-08:00","id":1014941,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Elfive</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1013866-hurt-locker?p=1014764#post1014764\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Does the Delta Protocol sound like a particularly legit operation to you?<br /> <br /> Also, you need to ration the stuff. It takes 2 days to heal a point of lethal damage, so with carefully timed withdrawals you can keep the attrition to a minimum.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> They definitely don't, but the Fixer merit is other Lost boys that have developed Serum. I just think the chart got mixed up between conversion with doses and weeks/months/hours. Always having damage on the track isn't a desirable thing for a super soldier (prototype). I almost would have preferred that Serum become like vitae or something similar, where abilities use points as you strain the implants. It would make management easier overall, and would give the knock-off serum an actual effect, like genuine Serum providing 10, while the knock-off only provides 5. This way you could make it a daily Serum usage dependent on your Protocol dots and kind of have it make a bit more sense. Do you really want to account for dosages every 6 hours in-game and decide whether you're going to go into Deprivation or Withdrawl? That seems like a lot more bookwork, where TOP already has a system that does it just as well otherwise.<br /> <br /> -----EDIT-----<br /> As a thought, using Serum like Vitae makes even more sense, as Serum toxicity only does bashing damage, it makes more sense for you to have to re-up in combat situations, otherwise the effect of a few bashing doesn't really affect you much. it would promote a bit more risk/reward gameplay.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":5761,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5761-shadowjakkal","user":"ShadowJakkal","date":". 12-09-2016, 04:52 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5761-shadowjakkal","name":"ShadowJakkal","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-09T14:15:33-08:00","id":1014955,"title":"","content":"I actually don't think it's that bad. <br /> <br /> At protocol 1, 0 dots of fixer is fine. Same with protocol 2 and 1 dot of fixer. At 3 dots, 2 dots of fixer is just about manageable (you'll have a perpetual 1 lethal unless you buy extra doses) and fixer 3 is sufficient (you'll need to spend a day deprived once a week). At 4 dots fixer 4 is fine as long as you spend some time deprived and at 5 dots fixer 5 is <i>exactly </i>what you need to avoid taking damage. <br /> <br /> So really, it's just fixer 2 that's the odd duck. At protocol 1 and 2 you need [dots-1], at protocol 3+ you need [dots]. So 2 is left as this weird limbo where it's too much for protocol 2 and not quite enough for protocol 3. And that might be intentional. It gives a leg-up for people who decide to brew their own to save a dot.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-09T15:20:32-08:00","id":1014970,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ShadowJakkal</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1013866-hurt-locker?p=1014578#post1014578\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">First, Wow, The Armory line books have always been good, and this is just another great addition. The Tag system is awesome, and I really like the &quot;merit templates&quot;.</div> </div> </div> </div>Just some pretty nice QoL improvements to the engine, aren't they? I'm really happy with this whole book and proud to have been a part of it.<br /> <br /> I don't know if I could choose a favorite part, but if I did, those scene frames are amazing. I use them for everything now, even noncombat scenes, and happily apply the whole idea to other games.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Freelancer </b>\u2022 Available for work!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/109-claire-redfield","name":"Claire Redfield","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar109_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"672"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-10T04:26:41-08:00","id":1015206,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Fumus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1013866-hurt-locker?p=1014622#post1014622\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I love the violent skills section, I think I found my second favourite line in any gamebook &quot;Drive: Bringing a Car to a Fistfight&quot; (second only to Trenchcoat McNinjasword from Danse Macabre).</div> </div> </div> </div>&quot;Violent Skills&quot;? What's this now?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>MtAw Homebrew:<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051456-even-more-legacies-updated-to-2e#post1051456\" target=\"_blank\">Even more Legacies, updated to 2E</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443819-new-2e-legacies-expanded\" target=\"_blank\">New 2E Legacies, expanded</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","name":"21C Hermit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12619_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3489"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-10T07:10:33-08:00","id":1015239,"title":"","content":"Would someone be good enough to briefly summarise the supernatural templates?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/321-sunlessnick","name":"SunlessNick","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1214"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-10T07:26:57-08:00","id":1015243,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>SunlessNick</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1013866-hurt-locker?p=1015239#post1015239\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Would someone be good enough to briefly summarise the supernatural templates?</div> </div> </div> </div>Right, We got:<br /> <br /> Atariya: people who have weird luck-based powers that can help them cheat death and stuff. <br /> <br /> Dreamers: Sleeper agents of some mysterious conspiracy who have become aware of their condition and can tap into their latent super-soldier abilities. <br /> <br /> The Infected: Carriers of a weird supernatural disease that can slowly mutate them into armoured, nigh-unkillable plaguebearers. <br /> <br /> The Plain: Supernatural pacifists that can spread their pacifism to other people. And take loads of punishment without dying and reflect it back at the people punching them. (Or if you like, carriers of a weird supernatural pacifism virus.)<br /> <br /> The Lost Boys: Deviant: the Prototype. You were a soldier. Some weird company augmented you with strange tech and then just kind of left you to do your own thing for no apparent reason. Might be some sort of experiment. <br /> <br /> Psychic Vampires: More or less the White Court from Dresden Files, only with less sex. You can suck health and willpower out of people and use it to augment yourself, heal, stay eternally young and a bunch of other shit.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-10T07:29:38-08:00","id":1015245,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>21C Hermit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1013866-hurt-locker?p=1015206#post1015206\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> &quot;Violent Skills&quot;? What's this now?</div> </div> </div> </div>They provide alternative 'violent' uses for various non-combat skills. This doesn't always mean doing damage; academics can let you destroy someone's social merits, for instance. Occult can also let you make weapons or other equipment that's suited to fighting specific supernaturals.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>SunlessNick</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1013866-hurt-locker?p=1015239#post1015239\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Would someone be good enough to briefly summarise the supernatural templates?</div> </div> </div> </div>Atariya: Supernaturally lucky people<br /> <br /> The Dreamers: Individuals who have been brainwashed/reprogrammed/otherwise conditioned for killing someone or performing a similarly awful mission.<br /> <br /> The infected: People infected by a supernatural disease that propagates through supernatural sources<br /> <br /> The plain: Pacifists that can make it difficult for others to be violent<br /> <br /> The Lost Boys: Augmented super soldiers<br /> <br /> Psychic Vampires: People that can and even need to steal bits of life/will through touch or eventually breath, and gain some abilities from it.<br /> <br /> EDIT: Elfive beat me to it! And with better summaries. Don't I feel silly. :P","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?affiliate_id=259490\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/themes/stvault/images/affiliatebanner4.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><br /> <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Christopher%20Falco&amp;affiliate_id=259490\" target=\"_blank\">Storytellers' Vault supplements (WoD, CoD)</a><br /> <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/FalconianP\" target=\"_blank\">My Patreon! (CofD bonuses include: Fae Sorcery/Technomancy for Vampires, Quick Conversion for Inferno, and more!)</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1130-falco1029","name":"falco1029","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1130_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1045"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-10T07:39:32-08:00","id":1015247,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>21C Hermit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1013866-hurt-locker?p=1015206#post1015206\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> &quot;Violent Skills&quot;? What's this now?</div> </div> </div> </div>It's a sub-chapter showing how the skills not directly related to combat (Athletics, Weaponry, Brawl, Firearms) cam be used aggressively. In fact, it even makes Occult useful in and of itself-you can use it, without any Supernatural Merits, to make temporary charms that give bonuses or penalties to supernatural beings. Even Academics, though, is a weapon of mass social destruction in the wrong hands (the more you dig up, the more skeletons you find).<br /> <br /> * SunlessNick:<br /> <br /> Atariya are people who have gained the blessing of a luck shrine, giving them the capacity to subconsciously manipulate fortune in extreme ways, which usually ruins their social life when and if they abuse it to win and keep winning (particularly given how <i>dangerous </i>happens around them a lot).<br /> <br /> Dreamers are Manchurian Agents with a second personality (usually an assassin) implanted in them by mysterious forces, but can access their assassin side's skills if they face breaking points (and in fact probably should, as if they run out of memory the persona activates and starts working towards completing a very nasty mission).<br /> <br /> Carriers are vectors for a semi-sentient supernatural disease that can turn fatal after ruining their social life due to the visible symptoms, but until that point it's also a symbiote that improves their health and actually makes them stronger the more acute the infection is.<br /> <br /> Plain Readers aren't truly a supernatural group, they're just followers of an online movement that preaches radical pacifism-except that something about that blog makes them preternaturally charismatic when attempting to defuse a situation, and some of them can even reflect harm back on people who want to hurt them anyway.<br /> <br /> The Lost Boys are soldiers who have been selected for experimentation by the Delta Protocol, gaining powerful cybernetic parts that the body does not seem to like, forcing them to take a serum that stops their immune system from killing them-but the parts also get more lethal in the initial stages of rejection, as the first to go are the inhibitors.<br /> <br /> Finally, Psychic Vampires are exactly that-people who for whatever reason have gained the ability, or an artifact that has the ability, to drain small amounts of life force (bashing damage and Willpower) from others; one of the biggest uses is stalling your aging so you don't actually get any older over the course of a year, but they have a set of other abilities that ape true vampires psionically.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.us/a/img824/1346/mosz.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/180-leliel","name":"Leliel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar180_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-10T08:54:25-08:00","id":1015259,"title":"","content":"Elfive, falco, Leliel, thankyou.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/321-sunlessnick","name":"SunlessNick","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1214"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-10T09:29:51-08:00","id":1015268,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Leliel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1013866-hurt-locker?p=1015247#post1015247\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> It's a sub-chapter showing how the skills not directly related to combat (Athletics, Weaponry, Brawl, Firearms) cam be used aggressively. In fact, it even makes Occult useful in and of itself-you can use it, without any Supernatural Merits, to make temporary charms that give bonuses or penalties to supernatural beings. Even Academics, though, is a weapon of mass social destruction in the wrong hands (the more you dig up, the more skeletons you find).<br /> <br /> .</div> </div> </div> </div>Anything cool for Investigation, Empathy, Academics or Science?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9102-whw","name":"WHW","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9102_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2542"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-10T10:28:54-08:00","id":1015292,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>WHW</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1013866-hurt-locker?p=1015268#post1015268\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Anything cool for Investigation, Empathy, Academics or Science?</div> </div> </div> </div>Yup. Every Skill is covered except Athletics, Brawl, Firearms, and Weaponry. Academics can be used to sabotage someone's livelihood, causing them to lose Social Merits permanently (they get the dots refunded with SoM but can't use the refund to buy back the Merit you sabotaged). Investigation lets you analyze a combatant's technique to gain one of a couple different Conditions that you can resolve to gain the upper hand in a fight against them. Science can be used to craft homemade explosives and chemical weapons. Empathy can be used to learn someone's Breaking Points and exploit them in Social Maneuvering, or trigger them to take the subject out of a fight.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-10T12:51:02-08:00","id":1015342,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Elfive</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1013866-hurt-locker?p=1015243#post1015243\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Psychic Vampires: More or less the White Court from Dresden Files, only with less sex. You can suck health and willpower out of people and use it to augment yourself, heal, stay eternally young and a bunch of other shit.</div> </div> </div> </div>Different families in the White Court feed on different emotions. The Raith family feeds on sexual desire/lust, whereas Malvora feeds on fear and Skavis feeds on despair.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2367-resplendent-fire","name":"Resplendent Fire","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2367_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1887"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-10T13:41:58-08:00","id":1015355,"title":"","content":"Yes, I know.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-10T17:25:01-08:00","id":1015421,"title":"","content":"Are there any new tidbits about Tokyo in the setting chapter?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11643-corax","name":"Corax","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"80"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-11T01:55:19-08:00","id":1015605,"title":"","content":"The setting chapter is literally <i>called</i> &quot;Tokyo&quot;.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-11T06:56:16-08:00","id":1015662,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Corax</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1013866-hurt-locker?p=1015421#post1015421\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Are there any new tidbits about Tokyo in the setting chapter?</div> </div> </div> </div>Oh, lots. Especially in culture, but the supernatural isn't neglected.<br /> <br /> Off the top of my head, there's a psychic doujinshi artist who unknowingly chronicles the lives of the real shadow world in her manga, and (my favorite) an onryo geist who's somehow managed to hijack the Shinjuku God-Machine and turn it into a ghostly station that gives its seekers a new life, at the cost of their current one being filled in by an unstable egomaniacal alien (she didn't do that intentionally, and in fact she sponsors a cult whose whole purpose is to control and eventually eliminate them).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.us/a/img824/1346/mosz.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/180-leliel","name":"Leliel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar180_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-13T10:16:03-08:00","id":1016624,"title":"","content":"I went into this book expecting it to be Armory 2E. It was not, but I still like most of the things I found in it.<br /> <br /> The new fighting style merit system is really cool, and I like that there are a lot of alternative style merits in there. The archery styles made using a bow not seem silly, though it is a bit confusing how they work with range bands, and I actually really like the Falconry set. I'm playing a mortal game set in 2030, so the Drone style could actually see use.<br /> <br /> The concept of Supernatural Merit Templates is really exciting to me, and I will probably have to homebrew a few of my own. I'm a big fan of Videodrome, so I really enjoy The Dreamers, especially Not A Bug But A Feature. I am a bit sad to see The New Flesh with The Infected and Holdout Storage with The Lost Boys for that reason. Some people in my RPG group don't particularly like the range band combat and cinematic ammunition stuff, but I actually prefer it. I'm a little confused over the explosives rules, but that is probably an errata issue rather than a design issue. If Hurt Locker had been out when my game started, I would have probably asked my ST if I could make my character a Lost Boy, since it makes sense with his background as a WWIII veteran.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12738-minty","name":"Minty","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"222"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-15T20:06:55-08:00","id":1017926,"title":"","content":"So, for the K9 Fighting Style, would anyone allow a Werewolf to get the fighting style and teach it to themselves or designate packmates in Urhan as the &quot;dog&quot; in the equation?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1127694-arcanist-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\"><b>My Homebrew Hub</b></a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4152-arcanist","name":"Arcanist","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1232"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-15T20:18:54-08:00","id":1017928,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Arcanist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1013866-hurt-locker?p=1017926#post1017926\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So, for the K9 Fighting Style, would anyone allow a Werewolf to get the fighting style and teach it to themselves or designate packmates in Urhan as the &quot;dog&quot; in the equation?</div> </div> </div> </div>Sure. I'd also probably allow K9 and Falconry with cainine and avian spirits.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":269,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","user":"Charlaquin","date":". 12-16-2016, 03:19 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-15T20:36:26-08:00","id":1017930,"title":"","content":"That's a pretty good idea. In general I'm loving all the Merits that let human characters push the limits on their Willpower storage. Hmm... Changeling with Hedge Beast Mount and Mounted Combat seems like another good combination.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1127694-arcanist-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\"><b>My Homebrew Hub</b></a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4152-arcanist","name":"Arcanist","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1232"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-15T21:47:45-08:00","id":1017950,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Arcanist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1013866-hurt-locker?p=1017926#post1017926\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So, for the K9 Fighting Style, would anyone allow a Werewolf to get the fighting style and teach it to themselves or designate packmates in Urhan as the &quot;dog&quot; in the equation?</div> </div> </div> </div>Never occurred to me, but that's kinda awesome. I'd totally allow it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>David A Hill Jr </b><br /> Freelance Writer<br /> Independent Game Designer","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/70-machineiv","name":"MachineIV","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar70_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1791"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-16T06:00:02-08:00","id":1018036,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Arcanist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1013866-hurt-locker?p=1017926#post1017926\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So, for the K9 Fighting Style, would anyone allow a Werewolf to get the fighting style and teach it to themselves or designate packmates in Urhan as the &quot;dog&quot; in the equation?</div> </div> </div> </div>I would love to see someone trying to &quot;teach&quot; a werewoof to do that, especially alongside a regular dog.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12738-minty","name":"Minty","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"222"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-16T06:11:22-08:00","id":1018038,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Minty</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1013866-hurt-locker?p=1018036#post1018036\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">werewoof</div> </div> </div> </div>I can see that as a slur among proud werewolves for those who are &quot;trained&quot; in such styles.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-24T02:17:41-08:00","id":1021501,"title":"","content":"Why do some merits have a + at the end of some prerequisites?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/904596-geniuses-and-gramarie\" target=\"_blank\">Genius templates</a>: Super Science Mini-Template for Demon: the Descent<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1337874-oracle-the-endbringers-fan-splat\" target=\"_blank\">Oracle the Endbringers</a>: Time-Manipulator Fan-Splat","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8331-milo-v3","name":"milo v3","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8331_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1505"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-24T04:32:45-08:00","id":1021521,"title":"","content":"Means &quot;or more&quot;, so if you had a two-form Merit that needed Strength 3 to buy the 2-dot version, and Strength 4 to buy the 4-dot version, its prerequisite would read &quot;Strength 2+&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#000000\"><b>Dave Brookshaw</b></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/14-dave-brookshaw","name":"Dave Brookshaw","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar14_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2081"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-24T05:35:53-08:00","id":1021537,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dave Brookshaw</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1013866-hurt-locker?p=1021521#post1021521\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Means &quot;or more&quot;, so if you had a two-form Merit that needed Strength 3 to buy the 2-dot version, and Strength 4 to buy the 4-dot version, its prerequisite would read &quot;Strength 2+&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>Except that doesn't seem to be how it works in these merits. Based on that, Cohesive Unit would have Presence 1+ as it's prerequisite, Peace Maker would have Wits 2+ and Empathy 2+. Which made me think it was the reverse of what you said. But Punch Drunk isn't a multiform merit and it's prerequisite are many more dots than the merit is worth, so I'm not sure how it fits.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/904596-geniuses-and-gramarie\" target=\"_blank\">Genius templates</a>: Super Science Mini-Template for Demon: the Descent<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1337874-oracle-the-endbringers-fan-splat\" target=\"_blank\">Oracle the Endbringers</a>: Time-Manipulator Fan-Splat","edited":{"userid":8331,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8331-milo-v3","user":"milo v3","date":". 12-24-2016, 08:40 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8331-milo-v3","name":"milo v3","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8331_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1505"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-28T12:36:18-08:00","id":1023381,"title":"","content":"I'm looking at the stats for the Lorica Segmentata armor, and I'm asking myself &quot;why did the Romans ever use this if the stats were just plain worse than the Chainmail?&quot;<br /> <br /> Let me break that down a bit. The Lorica Segmentata has an Armor Rating of 2/2, a Defense penalty of -2, and a Speed penalty of -3. The Chainmail, meanwhile, has Armor Rating 3/1, and Defense and Speed penalties of -2 each. This is also pre-firearms, so the Ballistic Armor rating on the right is essentially worthless because the only thing it does is protect against Armor Piercing, which almost no weapon provides and which the Chainmail still can equal.<br /> <br /> Was this just an oversight, or is Roman-era Chainmail different than the kind listed in Hurt Locker?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Revlid wrote:<br /> Yes, hollowing out your humanity to become an utterly utilitarian asura is the exact suggestion I would expect from you, Aiden.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/168-aiden","name":"Aiden","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar168_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1431"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-28T12:46:49-08:00","id":1023384,"title":"","content":"It was cheaper to make and easier to maintain, which is an important decision when talking about massive armies that travel.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-28T12:53:18-08:00","id":1023386,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1013866-hurt-locker?p=1023384#post1023384\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It was cheaper to make and easier to maintain, which is an important decision when talking about massive armies that travel.</div> </div> </div> </div>Except in Hurt Locker they list it as more expensive. Also my understanding was that the chainmail was harder to make but much easier to maintain, by comparison.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Revlid wrote:<br /> Yes, hollowing out your humanity to become an utterly utilitarian asura is the exact suggestion I would expect from you, Aiden.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/168-aiden","name":"Aiden","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar168_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1431"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-28T12:58:31-08:00","id":1023388,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aiden</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1013866-hurt-locker?p=1023386#post1023386\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Except in Hurt Locker they list it as more expensive. Also my understanding was that the chainmail was harder to make but much easier to maintain, by comparison.</div> </div> </div> </div>Now it's got a higher Availability because it fell out of use during the decline of the Roman Empire, while chainmail has been rising in popularity since.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-28T13:20:29-08:00","id":1023398,"title":"","content":"Yeah, the Availability reflects modern prices, and functional Lorica Segmentata is going to be pretty tough to come by nowadays. Mostly you'll get costumes and display pieces that aren't suitable as actual armor, and working armor will pretty much need to be made to order. Chain mail on the other hand is a popular craft, and while you'll still see costume pieces with ring gauges too small to work as actual armor, there is workable armor on the market and it'd be relatively cheap to have made.<br /> <br /> Availability aside though, Lorica Segmentata is still objectively the worst armor in Hurt Locker. Chain mail has lower Speed penalty, more body coverage, and 3/1 is strictly better than 2/2, even against firearms (a firearms attack that hits for 5 will do 1 lethal and 1 bashing to the guy wearing 3/1 armor and 1 lethal and 2 bashing to the guy with 2/2 armor). Plate armor has the same penalties and requirements but more coverage and 2 more general armor. Hard leather has the same general armor rating, better coverage, and significantly lower penalties and requirements. And pretty much all modern armor has significantly lower penalties and/or better coverage and armor rating.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":269,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","user":"Charlaquin","date":". 12-28-2016, 04:23 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-28T15:11:07-08:00","id":1023449,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1013866-hurt-locker?p=1023398#post1023398\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Availability aside though, Lorica Segmentata is still objectively the worst armor in Hurt Locker. Chain mail has lower Speed penalty, more body coverage, and 3/1 is strictly better than 2/2, even against firearms (a firearms attack that hits for 5 will do 1 lethal and 1 bashing to the guy wearing 3/1 armor and 1 lethal and 2 bashing to the guy with 2/2 armor). Plate armor has the same penalties and requirements but more coverage and 2 more general armor. Hard leather has the same general armor rating, better coverage, and significantly lower penalties and requirements. And pretty much all modern armor has significantly lower penalties and/or better coverage and armor rating.</div> </div> </div> </div>So this is why we have scenes like this with vampire elders. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> <div class=\"videocontainer with-aspect-ratio videocontainer-horizontal\" style=\"aspect-ratio: 16/9;\"> <a class=\"video-frame\" href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=VxmmRPISFNU&amp;t=140s\" data-code=\"VxmmRPISFNU\" data-provider=\"youtube\" data-height=\"0\" data-width=\"0\" itemprop=\"video\"> <div class=\"videothumbnail\" style=\"\"> <img src=\"https://img.youtube.com/vi/VxmmRPISFNU/maxresdefault.jpg\" alt=\"\" /> <div class=\"videothumbnailoverlay\"></div> </div> </a> </div>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-28T17:36:30-08:00","id":1023506,"title":"","content":"Can I just say how much I liked all of the Minor Templates in this one? I'd kill for more of those scattered into all sorts of upcoming books.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-28T20:44:06-08:00","id":1023566,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>atamajakki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1013866-hurt-locker?p=1023506#post1023506\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Pos