out The Dreamers in <i>Hurt Locker</i> than I have reading some entire gamelines, and I like tossing out player options that don't need whole Kickstarters and development team behind them.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-28T21:22:36-08:00","id":1023581,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>21C Hermit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1013866-hurt-locker?p=1023566#post1023566\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Like Dark Eras did with Skinchangers, right? Count me in the killing party, then.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah! I honestly felt more excited reading the section about The Dreamers in <i>Hurt Locker</i> than I have reading some entire gamelines, and I like tossing out player options that don't need whole Kickstarters and development team behind them.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-28T21:22:36-08:00","id":1023582,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>21C Hermit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1013866-hurt-locker?p=1023566#post1023566\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Like Dark Eras did with Skinchangers, right? Count me in the killing party, then.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah! I honestly felt more excited reading the section about The Dreamers in <i>Hurt Locker</i> than I have reading some entire gamelines, and I like tossing out player options that don't need whole Kickstarters and development team behind them.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-29T20:45:21-08:00","id":1024086,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1013866-hurt-locker?p=1023398#post1023398\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yeah, the Availability reflects modern prices, and functional Lorica Segmentata is going to be pretty tough to come by nowadays. Mostly you'll get costumes and display pieces that aren't suitable as actual armor, and working armor will pretty much need to be made to order. Chain mail on the other hand is a popular craft, and while you'll still see costume pieces with ring gauges too small to work as actual armor, there is workable armor on the market and it'd be relatively cheap to have made.<br /> <br /> Availability aside though, Lorica Segmentata is still objectively the worst armor in Hurt Locker. Chain mail has lower Speed penalty, more body coverage, and 3/1 is strictly better than 2/2, even against firearms (a firearms attack that hits for 5 will do 1 lethal and 1 bashing to the guy wearing 3/1 armor and 1 lethal and 2 bashing to the guy with 2/2 armor). Plate armor has the same penalties and requirements but more coverage and 2 more general armor. Hard leather has the same general armor rating, better coverage, and significantly lower penalties and requirements. And pretty much all modern armor has significantly lower penalties and/or better coverage and armor rating.</div> </div> </div> </div>The second paragraph here is my main complaint; I can get more out of the listed Leather Armor with Rating 2/0 and a Defense penalty of just -1 in a setting without firearms. The Availability point was admittedly me approaching it with the intent of getting use out of it for Requiem for Rome, so it skipped my mind to go 'oh right these are probably modern prices.'","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Revlid wrote:<br /> Yes, hollowing out your humanity to become an utterly utilitarian asura is the exact suggestion I would expect from you, Aiden.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/168-aiden","name":"Aiden","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar168_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1431"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-29T23:07:52-08:00","id":1024130,"title":"","content":"Keep in mind Lorica Segmentata are not particularly good armor, and historians are not even sure if it was actually used in battlefields at all. It is commonly accepted that by the end of the Empire legions all wore chainmail, and they probably did so for centuries. It's just that good.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12673-ew-matias","name":"EW-Matias","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"245"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-31T04:17:00-08:00","id":1024704,"title":"","content":"I'm dissapointed by Violent Skills treatment of Intimidation. I hoped for some interesting way to put high Intimidation dots into play and instead got a guilt trip attempt for putting dots into Intimidation and trying to use it, with an off hand note pretty much boiling to &quot;use the thing we cooked up for Empathy or whatever, its a dick thing to do why do you want to do it&quot;.<br /> Thing is, I don't necessarily want to do torture, and if you don't want me to do torture or to provide me with mechanics for torture, why are you spending 3 paragraphs of text on it? There are tons of other things that could be put under Intimidation and been given a mechanical spin to it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":9102,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9102-whw","user":"WHW","date":". 12-31-2016, 07:23 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9102-whw","name":"WHW","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9102_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2542"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-31T05:08:23-08:00","id":1024717,"title":"","content":"I think the intimidation section is less 'don't do it' as much as 'actually give this the gravity it deserves'.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/downloads/Backer%20Badge%20small.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/178-michael","name":"Michael","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar178_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3560"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-31T08:36:17-08:00","id":1024771,"title":"","content":"I think it was an important thing for Hurt Locker to talk about, given the unfortunate relationship RPGs have always had with torture, simultaneously perpetuating the myth that it is a reliable way to get someone to reveal hidden information, while also turning<br /> it into a game. I don't know if the Intimidation section of Violent Skills was necessarily the best place for that conversation but better to put it there than to leave it out of the book. But yeah, it would have been great to include a system for violent use of Intimidation that didn't involve torture.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-01T23:37:01-08:00","id":1025322,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>WHW</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1013866-hurt-locker?p=1024704#post1024704\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm dissapointed by Violent Skills treatment of Intimidation. I hoped for some interesting way to put high Intimidation dots into play and instead got a guilt trip attempt for putting dots into Intimidation and trying to use it, with an off hand note pretty much boiling to &quot;use the thing we cooked up for Empathy or whatever, its a dick thing to do why do you want to do it&quot;.<br /> Thing is, I don't necessarily want to do torture, and if you don't want me to do torture or to provide me with mechanics for torture, why are you spending 3 paragraphs of text on it? There are tons of other things that could be put under Intimidation and been given a mechanical spin to it.</div> </div> </div> </div>I agree. An RPG book isn't the place to tell me that torture is morally wrong. And for readers who do believe so, I doubt an RPG book is going to sway their opinion. Particularly one with a confrontational tone that advises players &quot;tell your Storyteller to fuck off if he says good guys can employ torture&quot;. I swear that's a near-exact quote from the book.<br /> <br /> Heck, if swaying reader opinions on torture is your goal (and it shouldn't be), don't even talk about morals. Four paragraphs in an RPG book is not going to make someone reconsider their likely deeply-held convictions in that area. Just neutrally explain why torture is ineffective at obtaining information. I still doubt it's going to win many converts, but torture's actual efficacy, rather than morality, is actually a pertinent subject for game developers to address in RPGs. Torture could well come up, and GMs could use a more realistic official system than &quot;roll Intimidation, he tells the truth if you win.&quot;<br /> <br /> That's the thing that really gets me. There was all that ink spilled over torture being bad, but no game mechanics to back it up. Just an author's &quot;you shouldn't ever use it&quot; essay, rather than rules for getting skewed information when you do use it. I've had torture come up several times in my current game, with PCs on the giving and receiving end alike. Skewed info rules would have seen use, if I liked them more than my own. Author condemnation of torture, however, is useless and provides nothing to enhance my games with.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://blood-and-bourbon.obsidianportal.com/\" target=\"_blank\">Blood and Bourbon</a>, my New Orleans-based Vampire chronicle.","edited":{"userid":3110,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3110-false-epiphany","user":"False Epiphany","date":". 01-02-2017, 02:40 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3110-false-epiphany","name":"False Epiphany","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3110_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"748"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-02T01:04:29-08:00","id":1025332,"title":"","content":"I agree it might be important to possibly include that text in the book...but I wouldn't sweat it not being included. Especially not in such place, at such time. It would fit perfectly as a sidebar next to the actual Intimidation entry. It really feels out of place to have &quot;How to manipulate and break people by gaining and betraying their trust 101&quot; laid out in neutral writing without comments on it being a terrible practice, and then suddenly get an anti-torture moralizing text...that refers you back to the Heart Breaking 101 for mechanical info. I think it's so jarring and clashing *because* of it, in fact, as both practices are abhorrent and terrible, but one gives you a useful gameplay-thing while second one tries to TEACH YOU A LESSON!!!111, then tells you to reskin another mechanic and be done with it.<br /> In a chapter which is supposed to expand your options.<br /> And the funniest thing is that the stuff that was written there isn't actually that relevant for the game and it's genre. &quot;It's not a thing that heroes should or would do!&quot;?<br /> <br /> Great. This is not a game about heroes, so...?<br /> <br /> &quot;Torture isn't at all like in movies and fiction!!&quot; doesn't matter. Because this is a game that emulates fiction where torture works, and often works *splendidly*. Where a good torturer will break your spirit and make you betray your comrades, yourself, and tell everything, knowing that you are sending your friends and comrades to death or worse. Intimidation entry should talk about *this*. And be contrasted by &quot;However, in real world...&quot; sidebar.<br /> Assuming that you want to put rules for torture in the game at all.<br /> <br /> The Torture entry is exactly what the book says it should not be:<br /> &quot;Any concepts and rules we present are designed to deliver stronger play experiences, not to teach you about human psychology. .<br /> Not to say that reading up on psychology and sociology can\u2019t help your chronicles, but any given shred of a topic addressed with serious, sensitive, real-world implications deserves more word count than we\u2019ve devoted to the entire idea of violence in this book. &quot;<br /> <br /> <br /> On a whole another note:<br /> Am I reading it wrong, or is Berserker Style basically &quot;pay 6 merit dots to trash your initiative, double your Willpower costs, yell at people while they slowly punch you to death&quot;? I could imagine taking the final dot of the style as a standalone merit, but everything else about the style - it's non synergistic costs, abilities that actually might do you more harm than good - makes me never want to pick this for character, or even play with it if given for free. Like, the best way to use this style is to hide behind your friends and yell at your opponents from the backline. That's not...what I think of when thinking &quot;BERSERKER!!!&quot;.<br /> War-Cry would be good if it was a reflexive action usable once per Scene, and the style should really focus on changing how &quot;Insane&quot; works on you, making it more and more beneficial state to be in.<br /> <br /> EDIT<br /> And no, I can't make it usable through use of Style Tags, because while &quot;attitude ENRAGED!!&quot; looks really cool as a tag, it's pretty useless, because there isn't a single entry tagged with it other than Berserker. Ditto for &quot;Movement (Strong)&quot; and Strength Performance.<br /> <br /> EDIT2<br /> Navigating the book in order to find persistent conditions and tilts is hard. Appendix that gathers them in one place would be helpful. Reading that Chronic Agony subjects the target to effects of Agony tilt doesn't really help me, because I actually literally don't know where to look for Agony Tilt. And I don't have much time, as I don't own the book and I'm literally skimming it f for content before having to go back home.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":9102,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9102-whw","user":"WHW","date":". 01-02-2017, 04:22 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9102-whw","name":"WHW","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9102_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2542"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-02T08:25:56-08:00","id":1025450,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>WHW</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1013866-hurt-locker?p=1025332#post1025332\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And no, I can't make it usable through use of Style Tags, because while &amp;quot;attitude ENRAGED!!&amp;quot; looks really cool as a tag, it's pretty useless, because there isn't a single entry tagged with it other than Berserker. Ditto for &amp;quot;Movement (Strong)&amp;quot; and Strength Performance.</div> </div> </div> </div>Kino Miutai has Enraged. And there's always the possibility for styles with these tags in the future. But yeah, Berserker is pretty bad, apart from Manic Brutality.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>WHW</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1013866-hurt-locker?p=1025332#post1025332\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Navigating the book in order to find persistent conditions and tilts is hard. Appendix that gathers them in one place would be helpful. Reading that Chronic Agony subjects the target to effects of Agony tilt doesn't really help me, because I actually literally don't know where to look for Agony Tilt. And I don't have much time, as I don't own the book and I'm literally skimming it f for content before having to go back home.</div> </div> </div> </div>The Agony Tilt actually isn't in the book. I'm sure it'll be added in with the errata.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-02T11:56:02-08:00","id":1025517,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1013866-hurt-locker?p=1024771#post1024771\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">But yeah, it would have been great to include a system for violent use of Intimidation that didn't involve torture.</div> </div> </div> </div> Curious minds inquiring - what would you have done? I mean, beyond the painfully obvious of threats of bodily harm?<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-02T16:16:17-08:00","id":1025615,"title":"","content":"Oh wow, I haven't noticed Kino Mutai because it has just Enraged, instead of Attitude (Enraged). My bad. <br /> Berserker is easy to fix, thankfully. I would play with the fact that character must go last when Insane and added some benefits that are get bigger as more attacks are thrown at you; some reward for the fact that you willingly accepting a potential pile-up. For the shout, I would just make it go off the round in which you activate the Insane Tilt - this would help survive the first round and make going last much more attractive. <br /> <br /> <br /> For the Intimidation entry - inspiring loyalty through fear that makes certain actions taken against you harder (like betrayal-proofing or making sure that no gang will accept a job against me); rallying your allies against something through use of fear (&quot;we fear the monster, but we fear the commissar even more&quot;); breaking minor mind control on yourself or your allies; scaring the shit out of your target so they underperform; projecting a subtle aura of authority that makes going against you in social situations much harder; making an example of someone to demoralize and discourage individuals and groups from target behavior. Etc.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9102-whw","name":"WHW","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9102_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2542"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-02T19:59:24-08:00","id":1025688,"title":"","content":"And there should be more than &quot;Using Intimidation violently is similar to using Empathy violently.&quot; Using Empathy violently is about learning what someone's breaking points are, and then using that knowledge against them. Using Intimidation violently could represent generalized techniques that become breaking points through their nature and repeated use. There could be focus on Intimidation making people <i>talk</i>, and then penalties on trying to determine whether or not the words are truthful representing how the victim's wretched state prevents tells and how the perpetrator's callousness clouds their judgment.<br /> <br /> I know it sounds sterile, but as it is there doesn't seem to be anything to support saying &quot;torture does not work&quot; with the game mechanics. As it is, if using Empathy violently &quot;works,&quot; (cruel though it is) so should Intimidation.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8064-mp122984","name":"mp122984","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"29"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-02T21:23:57-08:00","id":1025710,"title":"","content":"I haven't read that section yet, but it occurs to me that Empathy is about getting people to talk, Intimidation is about getting them to shut-up.<br /> <br /> &quot;Where'd you get that black-eye?&quot;<br /> Unbidden, the memory of his lover's fist flashed into his head. He stammered at the thought of what else, worse, awaited him at home...<br /> &quot;N... nowhere, I'm j-just a clutz...&quot;<br /> <br /> &quot;Did you see who shot her?&quot;<br /> 'Fuck no, man, I don't see SHIT around here!&quot; *Not while Copperhead still runs these streets, anyway*, he thought as he walked away from the pool of blood.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.dropbox.com/s/ofii86boiyk38ng/DtDRandomForms.zip\" target=\"_blank\">Open the gates of Hell: Random Demon Generator.</a><br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/1X6qQzoAPrSRNzl3cQcMWasoPv3eK56sIlAOTeay61No/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">Gather an army of Rage! Random Garou Generator.</a><br /> Shapeshifting Historian<br /> Writer - Werewolf: the Apocalypse, Werewolf: the Forsaken, Exalted 3e, TC: \u00c6on","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/167-nikink","name":"nikink","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"360"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-03T00:20:42-08:00","id":1025765,"title":"","content":"EDIT: Don't mind me I'm dumb misread something. <br /> Matter Mages gonna LOVE the Fine Art Of Overkill, especially if they are good enough to the point where they can reduce the size of ze bomb.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":9102,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9102-whw","user":"WHW","date":". 01-03-2017, 03:24 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9102-whw","name":"WHW","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9102_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2542"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-03T05:05:20-08:00","id":1025858,"title":"","content":"After checking out more of the Hurt Locker mechanics, a general comment:<br /> Good ideas, in some places good execution, majority is so-so, some are bad. Generally more good than bad, but nothing truly outstanding.*<br /> My biggest complain is that the book really, really wants to drown me in dice rolls - I don't like Extended Rolls and Contested Rolls because they involve too many rolls and in case of Contested Rolls, their results are even more unpredictable than normally and force me to account for tons of possible skill+attribute combinations for npcs. Playing this without an app that can resolve the rolls instantly sounds like a pace-killing nightmare. I loved the fact that NWoD tried to streamline the rolling into &quot;Create a Dice Pool, apply a modifier, check if there is 1 success, you pass or not&quot;; a lot of these mechanics stray away from that for no apparent good reason, other than just to be different. Like, why is the Watch And Learn a contested roll instead of a simple roll with target's Composure as a penalty? I feel that CofD could really gain a lot by shamelessly replicating Mage's core idea for spellcasting, which is &quot;Arrange a pool, and then trade your dice away for codified benefits&quot;, in other places.<br /> <br /> Overall: good, but in many places way too convoluted.<br /> <br /> *If you are not like me and don't hate opposed rolls that can mean having to roll total anywhere between 6 and 24 dice, and you don't hate extended rolls, and you don't hate the idea of <i>extended opposed rolls</i>, safelly &quot;upgrade&quot; the rating by one step for each one of these things.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":9102,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9102-whw","user":"WHW","date":". 01-03-2017, 08:08 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9102-whw","name":"WHW","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9102_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2542"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-06T01:37:52-08:00","id":1027495,"title":"","content":"Is there no errata thread for Hurt Locker or is it already closed?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1206-reiben","name":"Reiben","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-06T02:58:18-08:00","id":1027504,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>WHW</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1013866-hurt-locker?p=1025858#post1025858\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Like, why is the Watch And Learn a contested roll instead of a simple roll with target's Composure as a penalty?</div> </div> </div> </div>The general rule they seem to go by is that if # of successes matters, it's resisted. If pass/fail is all that matter's, it's contested.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3570-lnodiv","name":"lnodiv","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3570_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1607"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-06T05:44:25-08:00","id":1027561,"title":"","content":"Which brings me to another point: why are we back to wacky oWoD like situation where number of successes matters for something other than Success/Exceptional Success? (I know combat does that too. I personally feel it would be better if you only ever did Weapon Rating in damage, and had to take penalties to increase it for the attack instead of the situation now)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9102-whw","name":"WHW","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9102_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2542"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-06T06:10:52-08:00","id":1027576,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Reiben</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1013866-hurt-locker?p=1027495#post1027495\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Is there no errata thread for Hurt Locker or is it already closed?</div> </div> </div> </div>It's closed.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-06T06:36:37-08:00","id":1027596,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>WHW</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1013866-hurt-locker?p=1027561#post1027561\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Which brings me to another point: why are we back to wacky oWoD like situation where number of successes matters for something other than Success/Exceptional Success? (I know combat does that too. I personally feel it would be better if you only ever did Weapon Rating in damage, and had to take penalties to increase it for the attack instead of the situation now)</div> </div> </div> </div>So high accuracy (many successes on an attack roll) can compensate for low Weapon Rating? With some attacks there is a 0 Weapon Rating, so the only way you can cause damage is with Attack Roll successes.<br /> <br /> Still, your suggestion is a common house rule I've used to lower lethality.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-06T06:37:10-08:00","id":1027597,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>WHW</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1013866-hurt-locker?p=1027561#post1027561\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Which brings me to another point: why are we back to wacky oWoD like situation where number of successes matters for something other than Success/Exceptional Success? (I know combat does that too. I personally feel it would be better if you only ever did Weapon Rating in damage, and had to take penalties to increase it for the attack instead of the situation now)</div> </div> </div> </div>I think that would introduce another complication to combat that frankly doesn't need to be there, as well as reduce how lethal combat is, which would remove some of the allure of playing mortals, and have high level supernatural fights drag on way too long.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-06T07:33:29-08:00","id":1027637,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>WHW</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1013866-hurt-locker?p=1027561#post1027561\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Which brings me to another point: why are we back to wacky oWoD like situation where number of successes matters for something other than Success/Exceptional Success? (I know combat does that too. I personally feel it would be better if you only ever did Weapon Rating in damage, and had to take penalties to increase it for the attack instead of the situation now)</div> </div> </div> </div> It never left, and combat is merely one situation that it remained in. Number of successes still matter in a number of situations and rolls. For instance, extended rolls, like research or ritual magics, have always cared about number of successes. Someone else brought up contested rolls. Several powers in different game lines depend on number of successes - orginally Awe, from Majesty, was going to be based on successes again until people rightfully complained about how that was too random.<br /> <br /> Now, would the game be better off with having everything (outside contested) be a simple Dramatic Fail, Fail, Succeed, Exceptional Succeed? Possibly. But its not something we've gotten to yet. <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-09T19:13:08-08:00","id":1029422,"title":"","content":"You know, it occurs to me that a mortal magic user with the Object Fetishism Merit (or a couple instances of the Merit) would be a pretty serious threat, considering it gives them a substantial Willpower pool that fully refreshes once per Chapter, and that isn't tied to their typical Willpower pool. It makes the usage of magic a little more viable, and quite a bit more efficient.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1127694-arcanist-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\"><b>My Homebrew Hub</b></a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4152-arcanist","name":"Arcanist","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1232"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-10T13:44:04-08:00","id":1029732,"title":"","content":"Okay, I have a question about ammo and capacity. It seems that all firearms now have Bursts, either short, medium or long. Am I right in assuming that a short burst gives a +1, a medium +2, and long a +3? And what about the other benefits of bursts? And with these rules is a short burst the standard, as in single shots are no longer possible? <br /> <br /> Somewhat unrelated: the reload mechanics, is there anything stopping you from buying those reloads over and over again in a scene? (my knowledge on acquiring equipment is admittedly shakey, so this may be kind of obvious)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1752-mofous","name":"mofous","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1752_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"41"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-10T14:06:03-08:00","id":1029745,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Arcanist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1013866-hurt-locker?p=1029422#post1029422\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You know, it occurs to me that a mortal magic user with the Object Fetishism Merit (or a couple instances of the Merit) would be a pretty serious threat, considering it gives them a substantial Willpower pool that fully refreshes once per Chapter, and that isn't tied to their typical Willpower pool. It makes the usage of magic a little more viable, and quite a bit more efficient.</div> </div> </div> </div>So, you mean a &quot;sorcerer&quot; is encouraged to have lots of tools, implements, and the odd talisman?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-10T16:18:34-08:00","id":1029819,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>mofous</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1013866-hurt-locker?p=1029732#post1029732\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Okay, I have a question about ammo and capacity. It seems that all firearms now have Bursts, either short, medium or long.</div> </div> </div> </div>Note, this is only the case under the optional alternate rules for ammo capacity in Hurt Locker. But yes, under these rules, all ranged weapons with Low Capacity or higher are capable of burst fire.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>mofous</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1013866-hurt-locker?p=1029732#post1029732\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Am I right in assuming that a short burst gives a +1, a medium +2, and long a +3? And what about the other benefits of bursts?</div> </div> </div> </div>If you fire the whole burst at a single target, yes. With a Medium or Long burst, you can instead target multiple opponents (up to three with medium, or any number with long.) In that case you make a separate attack roll for each target, and each roll takes a penalty equal to the number of targets (and doesn't get the bonus mentioned earlier). You can also perform the Suppressive Fire maneuver with a medium burst.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>mofous</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1013866-hurt-locker?p=1029732#post1029732\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And with these rules is a short burst the standard, as in single shots are no longer possible?</div> </div> </div> </div>No, &quot;single shots&quot; are still possible. They just aren't necessarily narrated as firing only one round.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>mofous</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1013866-hurt-locker?p=1029732#post1029732\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Somewhat unrelated: the reload mechanics, is there anything stopping you from buying those reloads over and over again in a scene? (my knowledge on acquiring equipment is admittedly shakey, so this may be kind of obvious)</div> </div> </div> </div>Technically no, but the rules for reloads might be changing in the errata. If the change goes through, having extra reloads will be a Condition. They won't disappear after a scene, but you won't be able to stack multiple instances of the Condition. At most, you'll be able to have one instance of the Condition for each weapon you carry. If you want to be able to reload more than once in a scene, you'll need Loaded for Bear.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-10T16:46:16-08:00","id":1029826,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1013866-hurt-locker?p=1029819#post1029819\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Note, this is only the case under the optional alternate rules for ammo capacity in Hurt Locker. But yes, under these rules, all ranged weapons with Low Capacity or higher are capable of burst fire.<br /> <br /> <br /> If you fire the whole burst at a single target, yes. With a Medium or Long burst, you can instead target multiple opponents (up to three with medium, or any number with long.) In that case you make a separate attack roll for each target, and each roll takes a penalty equal to the number of targets (and doesn't get the bonus mentioned earlier). You can also perform the Suppressive Fire maneuver with a medium burst.<br /> <br /> <br /> No, &amp;quot;single shots&amp;quot; are still possible. They just aren't necessarily narrated as firing only one round.<br /> <br /> <br /> Technically no, but the rules for reloads might be changing in the errata. If the change goes through, having extra reloads will be a Condition. They won't disappear after a scene, but you won't be able to stack multiple instances of the Condition. At most, you'll be able to have one instance of the Condition for each weapon you carry. If you want to be able to reload more than once in a scene, you'll need Loaded for Bear.</div> </div> </div> </div>Thank you! Okay, so the rules don't mention how many single shots a weapon has, i suppose I could fall back on the original rules (revolver with 6), but I guess the assumption is that players will probably want to use those bonuses and eat up ammo significantly faster.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1752-mofous","name":"mofous","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1752_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"41"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-10T18:15:30-08:00","id":1029846,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>mofous</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1013866-hurt-locker?p=1029826#post1029826\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Thank you! Okay, so the rules don't mention how many single shots a weapon has, i suppose I could fall back on the original rules (revolver with 6), but I guess the assumption is that players will probably want to use those bonuses and eat up ammo significantly faster.</div> </div> </div> </div>There is no limit. You can theoretically make as many single shots as you want without running out of ammo. But remember, a Low Capacity weapon runs out of ammo on a failed attack roll, a Medium Capacity weapon runs out of ammo on a dramatically failed attack roll, and a high capacity weapon never runs out of ammo with single shots, but does jam on a dramatically failed attack roll, and a jam takes an action to clear.<br /> <br /> The thing about the alternate ammo capacity rules is that they are highly abstract, and chiefly concerned with running out of ammo as a matter of dramatic emphasis, rather than as a matter of resource management. Rather than counting each individual bullet and each magazine full of bullets, the alternate capacity rules assume you have a certain amount of extra ammo on you, and can reload between your turns as necessary, as long as you're keeping mental track of how much you're using, but gives certain conditions under which you lose that mental track and find yourself squeezing the trigger and nothing coming out of the gun but a clicking sound. Then, if you have the Condition representing extra ammo (not sure if David is going to go with &quot;Armed to the Teeth&quot; or &quot;Pocket Full of Shells&quot;), or the Loaded for Bear merit, you can spend your action on your next turn scrambling for that ammo and refill your gun. Otherwise, you're empty.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-10T20:05:12-08:00","id":1029886,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vent0</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1013866-hurt-locker?p=1029745#post1029745\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> So, you mean a &amp;quot;sorcerer&amp;quot; is encouraged to have lots of tools, implements, and the odd talisman?</div> </div> </div> </div>Well when you put it like that it sounds super obvious, but yeah, exactly. Magical practitioners take the time to bind various tools to their souls and draw on them for power. Bad things happen if they break.<br /> <br /> Actually, you could probably adapt the Rune Caster Merit from Dark Eras to represent any given occult tradition, more or less giving the &quot;sorcerer&quot; a Yantra too. There's probably a Style Merit in there somewhere.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1127694-arcanist-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\"><b>My Homebrew Hub</b></a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4152-arcanist","name":"Arcanist","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1232"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-11T17:24:23-08:00","id":1030341,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1013866-hurt-locker?p=1029846#post1029846\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">There is no limit. You can theoretically make as many single shots as you want without running out of ammo. But remember, a Low Capacity weapon runs out of ammo on a failed attack roll, a Medium Capacity weapon runs out of ammo on a dramatically failed attack roll, and a high capacity weapon never runs out of ammo with single shots, but does jam on a dramatically failed attack roll, and a jam takes an action to clear.<br /> <br /> The thing about the alternate ammo capacity rules is that they are highly abstract, and chiefly concerned with running out of ammo as a matter of dramatic emphasis, rather than as a matter of resource management. Rather than counting each individual bullet and each magazine full of bullets, the alternate capacity rules assume you have a certain amount of extra ammo on you, and can reload between your turns as necessary, as long as you're keeping mental track of how much you're using, but gives certain conditions under which you lose that mental track and find yourself squeezing the trigger and nothing coming out of the gun but a clicking sound. Then, if you have the Condition representing extra ammo (not sure if David is going to go with &amp;quot;Armed to the Teeth&amp;quot; or &amp;quot;Pocket Full of Shells&amp;quot<img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" />, or the Loaded for Bear merit, you can spend your action on your next turn scrambling for that ammo and refill your gun. Otherwise, you're empty.</div> </div> </div> </div>This makes a lot of sense. Thanks for clearing that up! I'd definitely be interested in seeing those conditions. As it stands, I'm not sure how I feel about these reload mechanics.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1752-mofous","name":"mofous","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1752_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"41"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-11T17:40:28-08:00","id":1030349,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>mofous</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1013866-hurt-locker?p=1030341#post1030341\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This makes a lot of sense. Thanks for clearing that up! I'd definitely be interested in seeing those conditions.</div> </div> </div> </div>I posted it earlier in the thread.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1013866-hurt-locker?p=1013940#post1013940\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><u>New Condition - Armed to the Teeth</u><br /> Your character is carrying extra ammunition for her weapon. Pick a specific ranged or thrown weapon when you acquire this Condition. By spending an Instant action and shedding this Condition, you can restore a weapon of that type that has run out of ammunition to full capacity. Shedding the Condition in this way does not grant a Beat. A character can have multiple instances of this Condition, each associated with a different weapon.<br /> <b>Possible Sources:</b> A character can acquire this Condition with a purchase at Availability one less than the Availability of the weapon it is associated with (minimum 1). At Storyteller discretion, a character may be able to get it by other means, such as robbing a sporting goods store or scavenging ammo off of someone equipped with the same type of weapon,<br /> <b>Resolution:</b> Have your ammunition confiscated or stolen.<br /> <b>Beat:</b> n/a</div> </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>mofous</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1013866-hurt-locker?p=1030341#post1030341\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">As it stands, I'm not sure how I feel about these reload mechanics.</div> </div> </div> </div>It's cool. They're an optional alternative to the standard ammo rules; if the standard rules work for you, no need to switch.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-11T18:18:44-08:00","id":1030367,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1013866-hurt-locker?p=1030349#post1030349\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I posted it earlier in the thread.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> It's cool. They're an optional alternative to the standard ammo rules; if the standard rules work for you, no need to switch.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'll definitely consider using this at my table. Thanks for sharing (again)!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1752-mofous","name":"mofous","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1752_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"41"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-11T19:04:14-08:00","id":1030381,"title":"","content":"The Violent Skills section on Intimidation reminded me of the Little Black Book from Reliquary in a <i>bad</i> way - both of them are moralizing lectures in the wrong spot.<br /> <br /> Seriously, I think that the whole lecture on torture would have been better off in Chapter One.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I have decided, after some thought, that I don't really feel happy on these forums. I might decide to come back to post. Who knows - but right now, I'm gone.<br /> <br /> So good bye, good luck, and have a nice day.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1170-amechra","name":"amechra","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1170_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2316"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-11T23:36:20-08:00","id":1030455,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>amechra</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1013866-hurt-locker?p=1030381#post1030381\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Violent Skills section on Intimidation reminded me of the Little Black Book from Reliquary in a <i>bad</i> way - both of them are moralizing lectures in the wrong spot.<br /> <br /> Seriously, I think that the whole lecture on torture would have been better off in Chapter One.</div> </div> </div> </div>Same here - Intimidation Violent Skill section should show Skill usage, not lecture STs and players. Like, I don't know, Intimidate with weapons usage - i.e. 'I have you at gun point' kinda scenes.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-12T01:44:28-08:00","id":1030472,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1013866-hurt-locker?p=1030455#post1030455\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Same here - Intimidation Violent Skill section should show Skill usage, not lecture STs and players. Like, I don't know, Intimidate with weapons usage - i.e. 'I have you at gun point' kinda scenes.</div> </div> </div> </div>Just read this section.<br /> Yikes.<br /> <br /> I don't buy books to be lectured about how the media improperly represents morally despicable acts. I would have loved a little more wordcount devoted to how to use Intimidation in other violent situations, though...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3570-lnodiv","name":"lnodiv","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3570_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1607"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-12T02:13:54-08:00","id":1030483,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1013866-hurt-locker?p=1030455#post1030455\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Like, I don't know, Intimidate with weapons usage - i.e. 'I have you at gun point' kinda scenes.</div> </div> </div> </div>That doesn't need any extra rules though, it's just making an intimidate check with the guns bonus included. It even happens in of the book's examples with an example of &quot;I am intimidating you at gunpoint&quot; and it has the dicepool as Presence + Intimidate + Gun's bonus - any appropriate penalties.<br /> <br /> Most uses of intimidate are already covered by the default mechanics, so this needed to add in something it couldn't cover properly yet.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/904596-geniuses-and-gramarie\" target=\"_blank\">Genius templates</a>: Super Science Mini-Template for Demon: the Descent<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1337874-oracle-the-endbringers-fan-splat\" target=\"_blank\">Oracle the Endbringers</a>: Time-Manipulator Fan-Splat","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8331-milo-v3","name":"milo v3","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8331_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1505"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-14T01:53:27-08:00","id":1031498,"title":"","content":"Page 52, Thrown weapons style, Impalement Arts (\u2022\u2022) mentions Impaled tilt. Where can one find it? Went though the CofD and Hurt locker books, but didn't see it.<br /> <br /> I wanted to post this in errata thread, but it is closed?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12856-spirit","name":"SpiriT","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-14T02:15:48-08:00","id":1031501,"title":"","content":"Oops. Yes errata has already closed. I'll make sure David is aware.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Writer. Developer.</i> <b>World of Darkness</b> | <b>Chronicles of Darkness</b> | <b>The Trinity Continuum</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/156-bunyip","name":"Bunyip","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1880"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-14T02:25:11-08:00","id":1031504,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Bunyip</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1013866-hurt-locker?p=1031501#post1031501\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Oops. Yes errata has already closed. I'll make sure David is aware.</div> </div> </div> </div>Thanks!<br /> <br /> I've been also creating a grappling character and some of the new Grappling style merits raised questions. Would be grateful to get second opinion on this:<br /> <br /> 1. Standing Throw implies that you are free to go prone with your opponent circumventing the usual rules, which require you to spend an instant action, right? And if you do go prone together with your opponent, isn't this actually completely same as using Drop prone maneuver?<br /> <br /> Just trying to make sure that the intended use for this it to actually break grapple by throwing your opponent on the ground.<br /> <br /> <i><b>Standing Throw (</b></i><i><b>\u2022</b><b>):</b> </i><i>Your character knows how to toss someone over his hip, trip, or sweep her while keeping his footing. He may inflict the Knocked Down Tilt as a grappling maneuver, but if he remains standing his opponent automatically breaks free.</i><br /> <br /> <b><i>Going Prone</i></b><br /> <i>When a character can\u2019t find cover, the next best thing when bullets are flying is to drop flat to the ground. Ranged and thrown attacks against him suffer a -2. A standing attacker using Brawl or Weaponry to attack instead gains a +2. A character can drop prone at any point before his action. Dropping to the ground costs his action for the turn, as does getting back up from a prone position.</i><br /> <br /> <i><b>Drop Prone</b>, throwing both characters to the ground (see \u201cGoing Prone,\u201d below). A character must Break Free before rising</i><br /> <br /> 2.Tap or Snap kinda requires Joint Lock to be a maneuver, but currently Joint lock sounds like it simply does one bashing damage every turn while in grapple and deals one additional lethal with any maneuver you use. Do you use it as some kind of a specific Hold maneuver with some damage?<br /> <br /> <b><i>Joint Lock (</i></b><i><b>\u2022\u2022\u2022</b><b>):</b> Once in a grapple, your character can administer joint locks and other immobilizing tactics. Any attempt to overpower your character causes the other character a point of bashing damage. Additionally, any successful overpowering maneuvers your character uses cause one lethal damage in addition to their normal effects<br /> <br /> <b>Tap or Snap (\u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022</b><b>):</b> Additional Prerequisite: Joint Lock Maneuver. If your character succeeds in a grapple in the turn after applying the Joint Lock maneuver, he may allow the opponent to choose between accepting the Beaten Down Condition, or suffering an Arm or Leg Wrack (attacker\u2019s choice) and lethal damage equal to the successes scored, as your character breaks or dislocates the relevant limb.</i><br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12856-spirit","name":"SpiriT","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-14T06:47:26-08:00","id":1031559,"title":"","content":"Seems like you're looking at the God-Machine Chronicle's version of Joint Lock, which mistakenly refers to the 1st edition grappling rules (e.g. &quot;Attempts to overpower&quot;). It got errataed in the CofD core book, now it says,<br /> <br /> <i><b>Joint Lock (\u2022\u2022\u2022):</b> You use joint locks and immobilizing tactics to limit your opponent\u2019s movement. You can use the Joint Lock move in a grapple. Next turn, your opponent suffers bashing damage equal to your successes. You can use Joint Lock as a lead-in to the Restrain move. In addition, any successful overpowering maneuvers your character uses cause 1L damage in addition to their normal effects.</i>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-14T07:08:45-08:00","id":1031566,"title":"","content":"That does raise another point though, Tap or Snap gives the victim a choice beetween the Beaten Down Tilt or the Arm or Leg Wrack Tilt and some lethal damage, which would inflict the Beaten Down Tilt. So, the latter is a strictly worse choice. In fact, since it requires a successful Joint Lock maneuver and Joint Lock makes successful grapple Maneuvers deal an automatic 1L, anyone who isn't immune to Beaten Down will already have it before you're able to perform Tap and Snap. Maybe the choice should be between Arm/Leg Wrack and damage or surrender, instead of Beaten Down.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-14T07:33:10-08:00","id":1031575,"title":"","content":"I agree with your assessment of standing throw, pretty sure the intent is just to allow you to remain standing instead of having to go prone with your opponent. The writing could use a little clarification, since breaking free is usually a reflexive action, but I don't think the intent is to circumvent the normal limit on actions per turn. Winning the grapple roll and inflicting the knocked down tilt counts as your action, and presumably your opponent's as well.<br /> <br /> I'm also not sure how it differs from Takedown, the second dot of the grappling style in core. The text on that one says &quot;You may choose to render an opponent prone instead of establishing a grapple&quot;, and unlike the Drop Prone maneuver it doesn't seem to require you to go prone in the process. It also allows you to inflict bashing damage, and can be enhanced with the Ippon maneuver to stun most opponents on 3+ successes. Overall it seems flat better? I guess maybe the difference is Standing Throw can be used anytime during a grapple, not just on the first roll.<br /> <br /> I strongly recommend looking up Clinch Strike for your grappler, it's in the free floating merits at the end of the section. Close Quarters Combat also has some good grappling moves, if you can get the prereqs and Tags to line up.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5328-helmsderp","name":"HelmsDerp","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"652"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-22T09:22:54-08:00","id":1036115,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1013866-hurt-locker?p=1031566#post1031566\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That does raise another point though, Tap or Snap gives the victim a choice beetween the Beaten Down Tilt or the Arm or Leg Wrack Tilt and some lethal damage, which would inflict the Beaten Down Tilt. So, the latter is a strictly worse choice. In fact, since it requires a successful Joint Lock maneuver and Joint Lock makes successful grapple Maneuvers deal an automatic 1L, anyone who isn't immune to Beaten Down will already have it before you're able to perform Tap and Snap. Maybe the choice should be between Arm/Leg Wrack and damage or surrender, instead of Beaten Down.</div> </div> </div> </div>Thanks for the catch! I indeed was looking at the older core book, not the God machine update.<br /> <br /> That's an interesting point, as it says &quot;<i>he may allow the opponent to choose&quot; </i>I understood that you can simply not give a chance. Allowing the choice is probably there to simulate the usage in official tournament, where the opponent would simply tap out and you don't want to break his bones.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>HelmsDerp</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1013866-hurt-locker?p=1031575#post1031575\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I agree with your assessment of standing throw, pretty sure the intent is just to allow you to remain standing instead of having to go prone with your opponent. The writing could use a little clarification, since breaking free is usually a reflexive action, but I don't think the intent is to circumvent the normal limit on actions per turn. Winning the grapple roll and inflicting the knocked down tilt counts as your action, and presumably your opponent's as well.<br /> <br /> I'm also not sure how it differs from Takedown, the second dot of the grappling style in core. The text on that one says &quot;You may choose to render an opponent prone instead of establishing a grapple&quot;, and unlike the Drop Prone maneuver it doesn't seem to require you to go prone in the process. It also allows you to inflict bashing damage, and can be enhanced with the Ippon maneuver to stun most opponents on 3+ successes. Overall it seems flat better? I guess maybe the difference is Standing Throw can be used anytime during a grapple, not just on the first roll.<br /> <br /> I strongly recommend looking up Clinch Strike for your grappler, it's in the free floating merits at the end of the section. Close Quarters Combat also has some good grappling moves, if you can get the prereqs and Tags to line up.</div> </div> </div> </div>Indeed, Clinch Strike is very neat, although it also overlaps with Takedown, as that move is pretty much also a Grapple opener.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12856-spirit","name":"SpiriT","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-22T10:14:19-08:00","id":1036143,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>SpiriT</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1013866-hurt-locker?p=1036115#post1036115\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That's an interesting point, as it says &quot;<i>he may allow the opponent to choose&quot; </i>I understood that you can simply not give a chance. Allowing the choice is probably there to simulate the usage in official tournament, where the opponent would simply tap out and you don't want to break his bones.</div> </div> </div> </div>Sure, but the problem is the interaction between Tap or Snap, Joint Lock, lethal damage, and the Beaten Down Condition.<br /> <br /> \u2022 Tap or Snap requires you to have performed the Joint Lock Maneuver first in order to use it.<br /> \u2022 The Joint Lock Merit causes all of your grappling maneuvers to inflict one level of lethal damage automatically.<br /> \u2022 Any amount of lethal damage inflicts the Beaten Down Condition.<br /> <br /> Therefore, by the time you can use Tap or Snap, the opponent will already have the Beaten Down Condition, making the choice meaningless in <i>any</i> context.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":269,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","user":"Charlaquin","date":". 01-22-2017, 01:16 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-22T13:25:05-08:00","id":1036242,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1013866-hurt-locker?p=1036143#post1036143\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Therefore, by the time you can use Tap or Snap, the opponent will already have the Beaten Down Condition, making the choice meaningless in <i>any</i> context.</div> </div> </div> </div>Excepting rare circumstances where beings might be able to downgrade Lethal damage to Bashing, but not be immune to the Beaten Down Condition.<br /> <br /> Death Mage Armor, beings with some form of Natural Armor that otherwise use normal Integrity rules, etc.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3570-lnodiv","name":"lnodiv","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3570_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1607"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-22T13:36:47-08:00","id":1036247,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>lnodiv</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1013866-hurt-locker?p=1036242#post1036242\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Excepting rare circumstances where beings might be able to downgrade Lethal damage to Bashing, but not be immune to the Beaten Down Condition.<br /> <br /> Death Mage Armor, beings with some form of Natural Armor that otherwise use normal Integrity rules, etc.</div> </div> </div> </div>Good point. That does still seem to leave the Merit with fairly narrow application, but I suppose that's alright.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-22T15:00:47-08:00","id":1036293,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1013866-hurt-locker?p=1036247#post1036247\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Good point. That does still seem to leave the Merit with fairly narrow application, but I suppose that's alright.</div> </div> </div> </div>Since the merit's in a book that specifies it's about mortals doing mortal stuff, I'd say it's more likely an oversight that <i>Tap or Snap</i> has limited mortal functionality.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Writer. Developer.</i> <b>World of Darkness</b> | <b>Chronicles of Darkness</b> | <b>The Trinity Continuum</b>","edited":{"userid":156,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/156-bunyip","user":"Bunyip","date":". 01-22-2017, 06:05 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/156-bunyip","name":"Bunyip","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1880"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-22T15:09:59-08:00","id":1036297,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Bunyip</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1013866-hurt-locker?p=1036293#post1036293\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Since the merit's in a book that specifies it's about mortals doing mortal stuff, I'd say it's more likely an oversight that <i>Tap or Snap</i> has limited mortal functionality.</div> </div> </div> </div>Seems like an easy enough fix though. Just make the choice between damage and arm wrack or surrendering (i.e. giving the opponent their goal from the combat scene) instead of Beaten Down.<br /> <br /> I mean, then it's still only really useful against an opponent who tries to keep fighting despite being Beaten Down, but that seems like a better niche than only being useful against characters who reduce lethal damage to bashing.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-22T23:03:20-08:00","id":1036453,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Bunyip</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1013866-hurt-locker?p=1036293#post1036293\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Since the merit's in a book that specifies it's about mortals doing mortal stuff, I'd say it's more likely an oversight that <i>Tap or Snap</i> has limited mortal functionality.</div> </div> </div> </div>More than one of the merits in this book allows mortals Armor that would put them in this exact situation. (Biomimicry, Bulletman Syndrome, Archangel System, Augmented Resilience, Sub-Dermal Armor, Nocturnal Supremacy).<br /> <br /> But yes, probably an oversight.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1013866-hurt-locker?p=1036297#post1036297\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Seems like an easy enough fix though. Just make the choice between damage and arm wrack or surrendering (i.e. giving the opponent their goal from the combat scene) instead of Beaten Down.<br /> <br /> I mean, then it's still only really useful against an opponent who tries to keep fighting despite being Beaten Down, but that seems like a better niche than only being useful against characters who reduce lethal damage to bashing.</div> </div> </div> </div>That seems like a good solution.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3570-lnodiv","name":"lnodiv","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3570_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1607"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-22T23:45:28-08:00","id":1036467,"title":"","content":"So. <br /> <br /> Just finished errata. The ONE thing that I wanted to do, but couldn't because of pagination issues and what-have-you, was include the referenced Agony Tilt, which comes up in a few places. I replaced those references to other Tilts in the final book, because I didn't have space for the additional Tilt within my given constraints.<br /> <br /> However, Malcolm was kind enough to provide the Tilt, so, if you want to use that in your games, here it is: <br /> <b><span style=\"font-size:14px\">Agony</span></b><br /> Personal<br /> <b>Description: </b>The character feels intense pain, above and beyond what's expected for typical physical trauma. The character suffers injury to a vulnerable part of the anatomy, an agonizing toxin, or a terrible illness.<br /> <b>Effect: </b>Reeling with pain, the character must choose between only one of the following options per turn: moving, performing an instant action (including an attack), benefiting from Defense, or performing a reflexive Strength or Dexterity-based physical action (such as resisting an attack or hazard). For instance, a character who moves may not attack or benefit from Defense. Characters suffering Agony may not perform the Dodge action.<br /> <b>Causing the Tilt:</b> The character suffers the following:<ul><li>Burns from acids or extreme heat (fire, red-hot surfaces) that inflict lethal damage in excess of Stamina.</li> <li>Further injury (1 point of damage, bashing or lethal) to an specified target already affected by a personal Tilt such as Blinded or Arm Wrack.</li> </ul><ul><li>Injury (1 point of damage, bashing or lethal) to a pain point. A pain point is a specified target category that encompasses the liver, genitals, armpits and similar vulnerable areas. Attacks targeting pain points suffer a -5 penalty.</li> <li>Certain special Fighting Style maneuvers and other circumstances may also impose the Tilt, such as certain insect stings, degloving injuries, or a maneuver that breaks fingers. Consult listed systems or the Storyteller.</li> </ul>Ending the Tilt: After the first turn, roll Resolve + Stamina as a reflexive action, once per turn. The player may spend Willpower to add dice to this roll. Success ends the Tilt, or it fades at the end of the scene. <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>David A Hill Jr </b><br /> Freelance Writer<br /> Independent Game Designer","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":8}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/70-machineiv","name":"MachineIV","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar70_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1791"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-23T09:07:39-08:00","id":1036669,"title":"","content":"Looks like something that could be put into a Death (and Life) Ruling Spell. I was going to complain that reflexive Resolve+stamina each turn will be too much rolling too often, but then I remembered that you basically can do only one thing per round, and thus the Tilt itself probably will cut out a lot of rolls.<br /> <br /> EDIT<br /> Actually, timing wise, when do you check for Resolve+Stamina roll? Imagine:<br /> First turn, I'm in Agony, can't do anything about that.<br /> Second turn starts. Do I get to check if my Agony is gone before I take any actions? If I get rid of it, can I move and take an action, apply defense, and so on? Or do I remove the drawbacks of Agony at end of the turn?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":9102,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9102-whw","user":"WHW","date":". 01-23-2017, 12:11 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9102-whw","name":"WHW","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9102_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2542"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-24T12:12:06-08:00","id":1037350,"title":"","content":"I pretty much have a lot of picks, but only one nitpick - 9mm pistols should be considered &quot;medium&quot; rather than &quot;light&quot;, so the example for light pistol should change.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/543-professor-phobos","name":"Professor Phobos","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"237"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-24T13:30:36-08:00","id":1037399,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Professor Phobos</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1013866-hurt-locker?p=1037350#post1037350\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I pretty much have a lot of picks, but only one nitpick - 9mm pistols should be considered &quot;medium&quot; rather than &quot;light&quot;, so the example for light pistol should change.</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't think there is a medium pistol category, but how would you make one? Would you make a category of light pistols with 0 base damage, or would you increase heavy pistols to do 3 damage and put medium at 2?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":12738,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12738-minty","user":"Minty","date":". 01-24-2017, 05:39 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12738-minty","name":"Minty","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"222"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-24T15:08:21-08:00","id":1037435,"title":"","content":"Generally everything up to, say, .380 ACP should be 1, your 9mm to .45ACP 2, and your bigger rounds (.357 magnum and up) 3, yeah. That's more or less the damage tiers for real-world pistols you'll find in most games, given the granularity level of the CofD.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/543-professor-phobos","name":"Professor Phobos","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"237"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-24T16:22:19-08:00","id":1037465,"title":"","content":"So if we go with the new categories, what would be the relative benefits of choosing a light pistol over a medium pistol?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12738-minty","name":"Minty","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"222"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-24T17:40:04-08:00","id":1037509,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Minty</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1013866-hurt-locker?p=1037465#post1037465\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So if we go with the new categories, what would be the relative benefits of choosing a light pistol over a medium pistol?</div> </div> </div> </div>Easier to hide and carry discreetly.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-24T19:34:43-08:00","id":1037585,"title":"","content":"How is bigger being defined? A .357 magnum is 9 mm. I can understand separated the two into different classes based on energy. Also, a .45 has been considered a heavy pistol for as long as the caliber has existed. There is no benefit to choosing a light pistol over medium. Even heavy pistols have compact versions for easier concealment. I think a similar discussion occurred during development and more categories of firearms was considered to granular.<br /> <br /> Edit: I am posting in reference to the handful of preceding posts.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1526,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1526-diggs","user":"Diggs","date":".  because apparently it wasn't clear 01-25-2017, 01:06 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1526-diggs","name":"Diggs","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-24T20:22:37-08:00","id":1037621,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Diggs</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1013866-hurt-locker?p=1037585#post1037585\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">How is bigger being defined?</div> </div> </div> </div>Narratively. A light pistol is a gun that serves the roll of small, easily concealed handgun. A heavy pistol is a gun that serves the role of big, high-powered hand cannon.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Diggs</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1013866-hurt-locker?p=1037585#post1037585\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">A .357 magnum is 9 mm. I can understand separated the two into different classes based on energy. Also, a .45 has been considered a heavy pistol for as long as the caliber has existed.</div> </div> </div> </div>If you think a particular model is better suited to one category than the other, go ahead and run it that way. The examples are just that. Examples.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Diggs</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1013866-hurt-locker?p=1037585#post1037585\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">There is no benefit to choosing a light pistol over medium.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's not true at all. Light pistols are size 1 to heavy pistols' size 2, meaning they can be used with only one hand and concealed more easily. Light pistols have a Strength requirement of 2 to heavy pistols' Strength 3, so more characters can wield one without penalty. Light pistols have an Initiative modifier of 0 to heavy pistols' Initiative -2, giving the light pistol user a better chance of acting first (and with the Beaten Down and Surrender rules, potentially ending the fight before the opponent even has a chance to use their higher damage mod weapon) than the heavy pistol user. Finally, a light pistoly may be more likely to have fewer restrictions on legal ownership and carry laws than a heavy pistol, depending on what weapons you decide fall into which category.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Diggs</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1013866-hurt-locker?p=1037585#post1037585\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Even heavy pistols have compact versions for easier concealment. I think a similar discussion occurred during development and more categories of firearms was considered to granular.</div> </div> </div> </div>I mean, Chronicles' weapon system doesn't have a ton of room for granularity. If you want to make a more granular system to use in your home games, have at it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-28T18:49:13-08:00","id":1039736,"title":"","content":"So as previously mentioned I really dig style tags, but they have one annoying downside, namely that they don't get used in other books and we're left to make our own rulings on styles not in HL going forward. <br /> <br /> To that end I figured I would ask people to weigh in on styles from other books and what tags seem appropriate. To start: Brute Force from Promethean seems like it would have the Emotion: Determined and the Movement: Strong tags. It's similar to Relentless Assault, which is a Determined style, and it has high strength as a requirement and calculates at least one advantage off that attribute.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5328-helmsderp","name":"HelmsDerp","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"652"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-29T05:52:29-08:00","id":1039950,"title":"","content":"Well, granularity limits being what they are, I just figure 9mm pistols should count as heavy, then, and the example light pistol should change.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/543-professor-phobos","name":"Professor Phobos","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"237"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-29T08:54:58-08:00","id":1040014,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>HelmsDerp</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1013866-hurt-locker?p=1039736#post1039736\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So as previously mentioned I really dig style tags, but they have one annoying downside, namely that they don't get used in other books and we're left to make our own rulings on styles not in HL going forward.</div> </div> </div> </div> Maybe? I mean, hells. Hurt Locker just came out. We don't know if there will be any tags in future books. Changeling may very well add a Supernatural tag to Elemental Battle for all we know.<br /> <br /> Look at Secrets of the Covenant - they added in Themes just to make it compatable with that book if people wanted. Future books might do the similar for Tags.<br /> <br /> Plus, I think most Fighting Merits out there are pretty self explanatory. The core book has been covered by Hurt Locker. Mage's fighting merits all rely on supernatural powers. (thus get the Supernatural tag). The new Fighting Styles in Secrets of the Covenant are all based on having organization training - that's pretty much the definition of Tactical tags; some, like Crusader, need more tags, but that's described fairly clearly in the merit itself. The only fighting merit in Changling is clearly Supernatural. Werewolf fighting merits are all clearly Supernatural (they have Renown / Primal Urge requirements) save Relentless Assault; the latter is mentioned in Hurt Locker under Attitude. Nightmare Fist (or whatever its called) is clearly supernatural. As far as I can remember, there are no fighting merits in DtD that aren't elsewhere. Lots of Demon Form merits, lots of combat Embeds/Exploits, but no merits that apply to combat directly to combat. Vampire's Kindred Dueling is Light Melee, and Frenzy is, well, Supernatural and Attitude (Enraged). Most of these are found in the actual description of the fighting merits, or the prerequisites.<br /> <br /> Tags don't really do anything but create a short hand for what can or cannot stack instead of relying entirely on explicitly stating it in the merit itself. Most pre=HL merits are pretty self-explanatory because they had to state it in their write up.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2102,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","user":"MCN","date":". 01-29-2017, 12:24 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-29T17:50:55-08:00","id":1040320,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Professor Phobos</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1013866-hurt-locker?p=1039950#post1039950\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well, granularity limits being what they are, I just figure 9mm pistols should count as heavy, then, and the example light pistol should change.</div> </div> </div> </div>I consider 9mm pistols light but the ammo optimized so they are roughly equivalent to a heavy pistol when it comes to damage. You can definitely change examples to whatever you like. Alternatively, you could keep a 9mm as a light pistol and boost the damage up to that of a heavy pistol when the appropriate ammo is used. Then again 1 damage might not be worth worrying about it. I presume the intent was to suggest that a 9mm pistol is typically smaller and lighter so would be easier to use, lower strength requirement and initiative penalty. Depending on what you consider important you can place it in either category. Maybe tweak it the way you want using light and heavy as guidelines for the range that covers common pistols.<br /> <br /> Tweaking seems to have been expected for those with the knowledge to do so with the examples made for those lacking. Examples, in this case especially, are suggestions not listed as such to save space. You've got it figured out, so go with your best judgment and you won't run a problem.<br /> <br /> I'm not trying to speak for authors. I've read what they had to say and expressing my opinion of their intentions.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1526,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1526-diggs","user":"Diggs","date":". 01-29-2017, 08:54 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1526-diggs","name":"Diggs","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-09T07:25:19-08:00","id":1046305,"title":"","content":"Looks like the final pdf has been released now that Hurt Locker has gone to print. Anyone notice changes? I see that Katanas still add durability.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Mage: the Ascension - <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1191028-redesigned-prime-sphere\" target=\"_blank\">Redesigned Prime Sphere</a>; <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1188769-simpler-wonder-creation\" target=\"_blank\">Streamlined Wonder Creation</a><br /> Mummy: the Curse - <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/474927-mummy-the-curse-2e-conversion\" target=\"_blank\">Lightweight 2E Conversion</a>; <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/22378-second-sight-tradition-disciples-of-duat\" target=\"_blank\">Disciples of Duat</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/61-octavo","name":"Octavo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar61_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1171"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-09T08:31:57-08:00","id":1046327,"title":"","content":"I never understood why Katanas add Durability. Extra durability for swords that literally had the problem of their tips falling of after striking something because they were so brittle and easily damaged? Wat.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9102-whw","name":"WHW","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9102_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2542"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-09T08:54:43-08:00","id":1046339,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Octavo</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1013866-hurt-locker?p=1046305#post1046305\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Looks like the final pdf has been released now that Hurt Locker has gone to print. Anyone notice changes? I see that Katanas still add durability.</div> </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>WHW</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1013866-hurt-locker?p=1046327#post1046327\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I never understood why Katanas add Durability. Extra durability for swords that literally had the problem of their tips falling of after striking something because they were so brittle and easily damaged? Wat.</div> </div> </div> </div>Depends where you look. The weapons charts in the actual equipment appendix got updated, the ones in the quick reference section do not (you'll notice the entries for Light and Heavy Revolvers are still out of whack in the quck reference page too). In the equipment appendix, the &quot;Sword&quot; entry just has +1 Initiative in the special features field, nothing about longswords, Jatakas, or durability. Why they didn't just change the Initiative modifier to -2 and leave special features blank, I don't know.<br /> <br /> It also looks like my Condition didn't make it in, which is too bad. But, pagination is what it is.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-09T08:59:03-08:00","id":1046341,"title":"","content":"That's really confusing. Why add +1 initiative to all swords instead of reducing the initiative penalty by 1?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Mage: the Ascension - <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1191028-redesigned-prime-sphere\" target=\"_blank\">Redesigned Prime Sphere</a>; <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1188769-simpler-wonder-creation\" target=\"_blank\">Streamlined Wonder Creation</a><br /> Mummy: the Curse - <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/474927-mummy-the-curse-2e-conversion\" target=\"_blank\">Lightweight 2E Conversion</a>; <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/22378-second-sight-tradition-disciples-of-duat\" target=\"_blank\">Disciples of Duat</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/61-octavo","name":"Octavo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar61_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1171"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-09T09:19:49-08:00","id":1046348,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Octavo</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1013866-hurt-locker?p=1046341#post1046341\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That's really confusing. Why add +1 initiative to all swords instead of reducing the initiative penalty by 1?</div> </div> </div> </div>Probably because David was going through a ton of errata and the only note he had on Sword was &quot;Still says Katanas get +1 Durability!&quot; so he took that part out and left the rest as it was.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-09T14:28:45-08:00","id":1046483,"title":"","content":"There's still some spelling errors and other weirdness in the updated PDF that came out yesterday. Is there still an active errata reporting thread?<br /> <br /> <br /> My group didn't end up using very many of the weapon changes in Hurt Locker. As far as guns and stuff goes, we ended up just revising the Armory (and Armory Reloaded) book to CofD rules, and added some small things like +P and +P+ ammo, magnum shotgun shells, revised hollowpoint rules, are other odd calibers. Melee weapons weren't hard, and ended up being pretty close to what was released in Hurt Locker anyway. Was actually pretty easy to do once both rulesets were checked out and compared.<br /> <br /> Transferring armor (like Dragonskin, or CTU kevlar clothes) was harder to do, and ended up with quite a bit of handwavium on my part. :-P<br /> <br /> Then again, my gamers like detail and action, and play a lot of Hunter, thus guns are a bit more prominent, so your mileage may vary.<br /> <br /> I have one guy right now playing with the Atariya rules. His character is generally a lazy, cowardly (but curious), slacker whose claim to fame was winning on The Price Is Right. He ends up often being the voice of cowardly but sensible reason for the group. It's really amusing.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/819-vaneheart","name":"Vaneheart","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar819_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"32"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-09T14:51:00-08:00","id":1046487,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vaneheart</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1013866-hurt-locker?p=1046483#post1046483\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">There's still some spelling errors and other weirdness in the updated PDF that came out yesterday. Is there still an active errata reporting thread?</div> </div> </div> </div>Nope, the update is the post-errata version of the book.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-10T03:14:50-08:00","id":1046698,"title":"","content":"Alright. Thanks for letting me know.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/819-vaneheart","name":"Vaneheart","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar819_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"32"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-01T01:03:04-08:00","id":1056528,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MachineIV</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1013866-hurt-locker?p=1036467#post1036467\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So.<br /> <br /> Just finished errata. The ONE thing that I wanted to do, but couldn't because of pagination issues and what-have-you, was include the referenced Agony Tilt, which comes up in a few places. I replaced those references to other Tilts in the final book, because I didn't have space for the additional Tilt within my given constraints.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's cool, but what about Impaled tilt? It's still in the book for Thrown weapons, but there is no description","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12856-spirit","name":"SpiriT","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-01T07:30:04-08:00","id":1056628,"title":"","content":"Should have been changed to the &quot;Pinned&quot; Tilt. The mechanics are in there they just got the wrong name.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5328-helmsderp","name":"HelmsDerp","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"652"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}